{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:00:38.378307Z","id":"93afd5ac8c780a1c47c30494a428a74153da243b8573252c1f6e38ce9f1bc60a","body":{"detail":"An artifact anchor could keep the serde default file (index.html) and let the shell skip it by kind wherever it matches threads to the page shown: the pin numbering and resolve request in web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts (numbers, resolveAll, selectThread) and pinPlaces in web/shell/src/view/pins-model.ts. That puts code in the artifact entry, which is at its gzip budget, and says the thread is on the index when it is on no page. With file empty every 'is this thread on page X' test is already false, and holds('') is false, so selectThread leaves the frame alone; only the lazy sidebar model, the CLI's is_detached and the summary needed the kind.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":37},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"725103793503edce275a0b1b4c87e30ea0156513acbd8424e83d38fe45bc5bd9"},"summary":"Whole-artifact anchors keep file index.html, with kind checks in the shell","tags":["revisit:a reader of anchors needs every anchor's file to be a published path","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/mentions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970855Z","id":"118a28f3a99f60c4c2b2bc0cec3aee2066562a29d6ff9058a4047275fda277a5","body":{"detail":"mentioned_in tries the whole run of name characters, then the run without trailing full stops. Without it, an @name at the end of a sentence would send nothing and be reported unresolved; a name ending in '.' (allowed by M22) still matches exactly first. Derived names never end in '.', '_' or '-' (names::sanitize trims them).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":69},"content_hash":"5e0108b81fa42f7b16bd97d7cef37870f0d47c6fe8fc1e7edbdab164d9bec3f3"},"summary":"@name followed by a sentence's full stop (\"thanks @web.\") mentions web, though spec §11 lists '.' among the characters that may not follow a name","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T02:37:42.970901Z","id":"b8dc8c7e6cfdd6721d4584d524357533ce628cca7d6364d241e9ddfa28d62522","body":{"detail":"token_form lowercases, applies NFKD (full-width letters, ligatures, the Kelvin sign fold), and drops marks and format characters (zero-width space, bidi overrides), but does not map confusables across scripts (Unicode TS #39 skeletons). Agent names are ASCII-only, so no agent name is a look-alike; only viewer and person display names are.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":99},"end":{"line":100},"content_hash":"b4f1af5a24ca1a764ea43e0d2e79e74679e3bb0a965b4c4f7372ad56af3f5841"},"suggested_fix":"Compare UTS #39 skeletons of display names in check_viewer_name and check_person_name, or limit the refusal to mixed-script names.","summary":"Display names in other scripts that look like a person's (Cyrillic 'Ѕаm' for 'Sam') are different names: a LAN viewer can take one","tags":["security","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.121472Z","id":"514ec4a99511e3cea22a1cbeee57c9edfabba8c026974ce0aea1d112b4f95a32","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b8dc8c7e6cfdd6721d4584d524357533ce628cca7d6364d241e9ddfa28d62522","summary":"Same-script invisible characters and bidi overrides also bypass the check, which makes the section 9.6 refusal easy to evade; see the concern on crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:35:46","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.121987Z","id":"864d683593e4201b6ba0901ae64d9024308e500e894684d7b0a93180526119b0","body":{"detail":"Spec section 11 takes the basename of the directory holding .git, a worktree's file included; repo_and_branch does so. For this repository's worktree .claude/worktrees/multi-person on branch multi-person that gives repo 'multi-person' and the name 'multi-person-multi-person'. Spec section 3.5 names the owner's agents `clax-main` (Claude Code in clax) and `clax-multi-person` (Codex in a worktree), and section 19 item 1 uses `clax-main`; under section 11, clax on main is `clax`, which is reserved, so it is `clax-claude`. The normative text and the examples disagree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":153},"end":{"line":194},"content_hash":"d7b2278d0bb90cec01364ca1c9d08674ff15fa69086e6480728e153c2d14075b"},"suggested_fix":"Decide one of: (a) for a worktree, take the repository name from its common git directory (the gitdir line's <repo>/.git/worktrees/<n>, or its commondir file) and amend section 11, which gives clax-multi-person here; (b) keep section 11 and fix the section 3.5 and 19 examples. Either way, fix the clax-main examples.","summary":"A worktree is named after its own directory, so a Claude Code worktree gets a doubled name (multi-person-multi-person), while spec section 3.5 expects clax-multi-person","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","spec:11","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/mentions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:09.122064Z","id":"08e57e0e2466c9c214d67025ae90f034cce6f3268425c040bb6b1d1800910924","body":{"detail":"'.' after a name is excluded so @web.dev never mentions web; that still holds, since the run is maximal and only trailing full stops are trimmed. set_session_name accepts names ending in '.', '_' or '-' (crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:475; M22 allows them) though derived names never end so; with 'web' and 'web.' both live, 'thanks @web.' reaches 'web.'. Refusing such endings for chosen names removes the ambiguity.","kind":"comment","references":"118a28f3a99f60c4c2b2bc0cec3aee2066562a29d6ff9058a4047275fda277a5","summary":"Reviewer's recommendation: keep the sentence-stop reading and amend spec section 11; refuse chosen names that end in '.', '_' or '-'","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.467860Z","id":"b26e3a31e3daea0db9b3a81760b4c7fbfd323af28f62f53420429e28c43950e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbf0fe7","summary":"Fixed in dbf0fe7: checked_name refuses bidirectional controls and mixed-script names (names::is_mixed_script: Latin with Cyrillic, Greek or another script; Latin with Han and kana, Bopomofo or Hangul allowed), and token_form drops default-ignorable characters and reads U+2800 as a space. crates/clax-server/tests/api_viewers.rs names_that_render_as_a_persons_or_the_owners_are_refused refuses every probe of the Task 7 review (bidi override, RLM, isolates, Hangul fillers, braille blank, Cyrillic and Greek look-alikes, full-width, ZWSP, variation selector, tag character, CGJ, NUL, newline); names::tests cover the helpers. A name wholly in another script that looks Latin is still a different name.","supersedes":"b8dc8c7e6cfdd6721d4584d524357533ce628cca7d6364d241e9ddfa28d62522","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/mentions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.467933Z","id":"92abe45f2cd6a25f838a92f2a78923a07e88a60385a632d24f08c8e98a9a7afd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbf0fe7","summary":"The owner decided: \"a sentence's closing full stop isn't part of the name, so @web. mentions web. Together with the m3 change (names can't end in ., _ or -), that leaves nothing ambiguous. Amend §11.\" §11 amended and chosen names refused a trailing ., _ or - in dbf0fe7; tests mentions::tests::agent_mentions_match_whole_live_names_at_a_boundary and sessions::tests::names::chosen_names_must_have_the_m22_form.","supersedes":"118a28f3a99f60c4c2b2bc0cec3aee2066562a29d6ff9058a4047275fda277a5","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:21:50.468Z","id":"3375ad58eea8ee3d888ed7f5698f536e13730019c808d91169c05ee4498c0ed3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dbf0fe7","summary":"The owner decided: \"take the repository name from the common git directory (git rev-parse --git-common-dir, its parent's directory name), so a worktree's agent is named after the repository. Amend §11, and fix the spec's clax-main examples to the names the rule actually derives.\" Implemented in dbf0fe7 (names::repo_and_branch reads the worktree's commondir; a bare repository's common directory gives its own name without .git); §11 amended and §3.5, §13, §14 and §19 examples now say clax-claude. Test names::tests::repository_and_branch_are_read_from_git_files covers a main checkout, a worktree, a worktree without commondir, and a bare repository's worktree.","supersedes":"864d683593e4201b6ba0901ae64d9024308e500e894684d7b0a93180526119b0","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:09.171977Z","id":"39f2474c4c48b2472b006d7bc5b05ba128e3a6d5f40a8a69a458318cc8d3e961","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b26e3a31e3daea0db9b3a81760b4c7fbfd323af28f62f53420429e28c43950e2","summary":"The accepted residual (a name wholly in another script that looks Latin, such as 'АЛЕХ' or 'ΑΒΕ', is accepted) lives only in this resolve's summary; a waiver on names::is_mixed_script would keep it visible","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/mentions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:22.293991Z","id":"341473f4baa702e81a9de48f1e89fd858c79c718e9518fba31d38d4b6b49b854","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"92abe45f2cd6a25f838a92f2a78923a07e88a60385a632d24f08c8e98a9a7afd","summary":"This resolve records the owner's decision, which the owner gave in the coordinating session on 2026-10-10; the owner did not write the record, an agent did.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:37:22.294010Z","id":"f9a4b5657160d5a404c34643fe2d44f17dcdc882782df4241d9c8e0f4e856b70","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3375ad58eea8ee3d888ed7f5698f536e13730019c808d91169c05ee4498c0ed3","summary":"This resolve records the owner's decision, which the owner gave in the coordinating session on 2026-10-10; the owner did not write the record, an agent did.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/mentions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:45:31.444783Z","id":"82c710cbef839f937ac1a119571f098c2b5e4933c116703d92eb1611cd664deb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"92abe45f2cd6a25f838a92f2a78923a07e88a60385a632d24f08c8e98a9a7afd","summary":"Closed by an agent on the owner's decision, recorded 2026-10-10.","supersedes":"341473f4baa702e81a9de48f1e89fd858c79c718e9518fba31d38d4b6b49b854","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:45:31.444876Z","id":"c50b7ce5d9c63d3799c176cc2c351133bd2d2264b71810767485eb61adc724ed","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3375ad58eea8ee3d888ed7f5698f536e13730019c808d91169c05ee4498c0ed3","summary":"Closed by an agent on the owner's decision, recorded 2026-10-10.","supersedes":"f9a4b5657160d5a404c34643fe2d44f17dcdc882782df4241d9c8e0f4e856b70","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T04:45:31.444955Z","id":"2a37f2463b36e9cdfd4834cb5aa86d4568bf16bb44aa834356322d632cdb86b7","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"39f2474c4c48b2472b006d7bc5b05ba128e3a6d5f40a8a69a458318cc8d3e961","summary":"Correction: names::is_mixed_script no longer exists. Since 10b9ae1, display names may use any script, and a name that looks like a protected one collides by UTS #39 skeleton (names::CollisionKeys), so whole-script look-alikes such as all-Cyrillic 'Сосо' for 'Coco' are name_taken (names::tests::look_alike_names_meet). 'АЛЕХ' does not collide with 'Alex': UTS #39 maps Cyrillic Л to ʌ, not L.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:49:07.080762Z","id":"f14e00da3d1ced5cf2bdae4d94f5c18c2bc8c16148711c9be03a90ff3dde7ff4","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs writes resolved_by as viewer:<public ID>, viewer:anonymous or agent:<harness>. Spec §8.2 makes a thread's resolved_by text the resolver's, but an agent resolve keeps neither its session nor its person, so the filter cannot tell Sam's agent from the owner's: it is withheld from every person's agents and reaches the owner's agents only through the *unconnected approval. The text itself is a harness name, so nothing an author wrote leaks either way; the cost is a placeholder where the owner's own agent resolved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"27c2c66e0c360e0aca0c6eec67a6311feb1e5590c9bcfb3d6f1ac9000812c07d"},"suggested_fix":"When the thread routes are filtered, record the resolving agent's person with the resolve (for example agent:<harness>:<public ID or *owner>, or a resolved_by_person column) and map it in authors_of_resolved_by.","summary":"An agent's resolve is stored as resolved_by 'agent:<harness>', which names no session or person, so authors_of_resolved_by counts it as *unconnected","tags":["visibility","revisit:when the thread routes are filtered per field","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:49:07.080892Z","id":"ae90d3ccadc9eea72502bd1f394445df9e85451a5f8339f9ef7cfe1c7a1fb4ed","body":{"detail":"Spec §8.2 makes a batch note's authors its sender. crates/clax-core/src/store/batches.rs stores sent_by as the name from the route's author() (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs send_batch), and migration 25 (spec §5.2) adds no column for the sender's public ID, so authors_of_batch_note takes the public ID from its caller, which no row can supply yet. Mapping the name back to a viewer is unsafe: names are not unique among LAN viewers.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"66138ffbfb4fb352c38d43f56eb5574bfff56af8b20efb67756861df5b9ce7c3"},"suggested_fix":"Store the sender's public ID with the batch (a send_batches column, NULL for existing rows read as the owner, who sent every batch before people existed), set by the batch send route, and amend spec §5.2.","summary":"A batch's note has no sender ID to filter by: send_batches.sent_by holds the sender's display name, not a public ID","tags":["visibility","status:needs-decision","spec-gap","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T15:49:07.080977Z","id":"2859f2a857584daf17c95921785feb5baf64eef3fd6f18e382c0caf8cecf57ca","body":{"detail":"authors_of_comment takes an agent comment's author from its session's person (comments.via_session_id joined to sessions.person, Comment.agent_person). Comments carry no person of their own, so an agent comment written with via_session_id NULL reads as the owner's. The owner's agents' sessionless replies are correct as the owner's; a PersonAgent without a session (spec §6.7 makes the session optional) is not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"c3227d4af872cfbbfc578e1f98c440fea17cf2423a068e5baf362f056e7ae0aa"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse agent replies from a PersonAgent without a session, or store the replying person on the comment (comments.person), before the thread routes are filtered.","summary":"An agent comment with no session counts as the owner's: a person's agent replying without X-Clax-Session would have its words reach the owner's agents unapproved","tags":["visibility","revisit:when the agent reply route is filtered","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:44:26.965120Z","id":"5de51d9f594c428f7feb8c5840e85d75559d045c63f06dccabea2bdb507e9af7","body":{"detail":"Migration 25 is not on main and no home has run it, so the column can join it rather than take a new number (M27). Store the sender as an author token ('*owner', a public ID, or '*unconnected' for an anonymous browser), set by the send_batch route from the caller (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs send_batch), keeping sent_by as the display name for views. Read NULL (rows before the migration) as *unconnected, not the owner: send_batch takes LAN viewers' browser requests, so an old note may be a LAN viewer's; on a single-owner install with the switch on that changes nothing, and a person's agent gets a placeholder rather than a LAN viewer's note passed off as the owner's. authors_of_batch_note then takes the token. Amend spec §5.2 and §8.2's batch-note row.","kind":"comment","references":"ae90d3ccadc9eea72502bd1f394445df9e85451a5f8339f9ef7cfe1c7a1fb4ed","summary":"Recommendation: add send_batches.sender (an author token) to migration 25, and read existing rows as *unconnected","tags":["review","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:48:36.827514Z","id":"fa223a910b69b3590b0bc5f571d4a63a951e2ed17c624f2bbe3f67ade5e5550f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7442e6d","summary":"Fixed as the coordinator ruled (following reply 5de51d9f): migration 25 gains send_batches.sender in place, an author token ('*owner', a public ID, or '*unconnected') set by the send_batch route from the caller (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs); sent_by stays the display name; rows without a sender read as *unconnected (authors_of_batch_note). Spec §5.2 and §8.2 amended. Evidence: visibility::tests::a_batch_note_is_its_sender_s and a_fold_moves_every_authorship_column pass; cargo nextest run --workspace at 7442e6d, 1901 passed.","supersedes":"ae90d3ccadc9eea72502bd1f394445df9e85451a5f8339f9ef7cfe1c7a1fb4ed","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.377791Z","id":"27bb653db0c9d441e4dbb4993dd5e71be6bfbeb9c6e7136e0e7378ae0b7c366f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs writes resolved_by as viewer:<public ID>, viewer:anonymous or agent:<harness>. Spec §8.2 makes a thread's resolved_by text the resolver's, but an agent resolve keeps neither its session nor its person, so the filter cannot tell Sam's agent from the owner's: it is withheld from every person's agents and reaches the owner's agents only through the *unconnected approval. The text itself is a harness name, so nothing an author wrote leaks either way; the cost is a placeholder where the owner's own agent resolved.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":167},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"27c2c66e0c360e0aca0c6eec67a6311feb1e5590c9bcfb3d6f1ac9000812c07d"},"suggested_fix":"When the thread routes are filtered, record the resolving agent's person with the resolve (for example agent:<harness>:<public ID or *owner>, or a resolved_by_person column) and map it in authors_of_resolved_by.","summary":"An agent's resolve is stored as resolved_by 'agent:<harness>', which names no session or person, so authors_of_resolved_by counts it as *unconnected","supersedes":"f14e00da3d1ced5cf2bdae4d94f5c18c2bc8c16148711c9be03a90ff3dde7ff4","tags":["visibility","revisit:when the thread routes are filtered per field","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:49:00.378725Z","id":"6dd12ea23d6a2e95491bd0a71e7b9d575d86ef5f6fda9f2848ede5542c8fdb8f","body":{"detail":"authors_of_comment takes an agent comment's author from its session's person (comments.via_session_id joined to sessions.person, Comment.agent_person). Comments carry no person of their own, so an agent comment written with via_session_id NULL reads as the owner's. The owner's agents' sessionless replies are correct as the owner's; a PersonAgent without a session (spec §6.7 makes the session optional) is not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"d50d2492d1940eafd491528517ed475ef51f26b2def8a9795d2449777ca56adc"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse agent replies from a PersonAgent without a session, or store the replying person on the comment (comments.person), before the thread routes are filtered.","summary":"An agent comment with no session counts as the owner's: a person's agent replying without X-Clax-Session would have its words reach the owner's agents unapproved","supersedes":"2859f2a857584daf17c95921785feb5baf64eef3fd6f18e382c0caf8cecf57ca","tags":["visibility","revisit:when the agent reply route is filtered","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T19:56:33.607717Z","id":"6592889ad8411a565f939a869949203b1cb964a3b5e23ed0ef9010aa8bfce2e8","body":{"detail":"A thread anchored on the whole artifact (anchor kind artifact, crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs is_whole) has file \"\" and quote, prefix, suffix and selector all null. authors_of_anchor looks up file_authors for \"\", finds none, and falls back to the version's publisher (file_authors, crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:134:145). When Task 9 filters threads by these authors, a reader who may not see the publisher gets anchor_withheld: true (Withhold::anchor) on an anchor that has nothing to withhold. The comments' authors are unaffected: a whole-artifact comment is credited like any other (authors_of_comment), and a page cannot make one (crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs refuses via_page with an artifact anchor).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":147},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"2157d4da24997df61407122c0325d49ff023870401afd81ca6dc23a2a9758fe9"},"suggested_fix":"Return no authors from authors_of_anchor (and so from the anchor part of authors_of_clip) when thread.anchor.is_whole(), and pin it in the thread filter's tests.","summary":"A whole-artifact thread's anchor is credited to the version's publisher, so it is marked anchor_withheld for readers who may not see the publisher though it holds no text","tags":["people","visibility","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.888446Z","id":"85bf16add8584cca24e5c1d57f58bd4823e05c78461281fa2d15d8f5c15abcfa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:9bf6584","summary":"A person's agent can no longer write a comment without a session: crates/clax-server/src/routes/threads.rs person_agent_comments answers 400 no_session for every comment and thread write of a Clax-Grant caller with no X-Clax-Session (spec §6.7). Test: cargo test -p clax-server --test integration api_visibility::a_persons_agent_comments_from_a_session_as_its_person passes.","supersedes":"6dd12ea23d6a2e95491bd0a71e7b9d575d86ef5f6fda9f2848ede5542c8fdb8f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.888610Z","id":"f750c9d0342401862307466ec5a67a6b7284b4a5978950832992208e90ca1b9e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:45d8d5a","summary":"authors_of_anchor returns no authors for a whole-artifact anchor. Tests: visibility::tests::a_whole_artifact_anchor_has_no_authors_so_is_never_withheld and api_visibility::a_whole_artifact_thread_on_anothers_page_withholds_no_anchor pass.","supersedes":"6592889ad8411a565f939a869949203b1cb964a3b5e23ed0ef9010aa8bfce2e8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T20:36:09.888772Z","id":"caec06d10516ce98353e97e9679e3f628cb3d3224b77a7728dd664322d2556a4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:45d8d5a","summary":"threads.resolved_by_person (migration 25) records the resolving agent's person and authors_of_resolved_by reads it. Tests: visibility::tests::an_agents_resolve_keeps_its_person_until_the_thread_reopens and api_visibility::an_agents_resolve_is_its_persons pass.","supersedes":"27bb653db0c9d441e4dbb4993dd5e71be6bfbeb9c6e7136e0e7378ae0b7c366f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T05:51:18.822757Z","id":"7fdbaaf50ad63d42fc3fd4a60db63c388e863bc07db94901a2863ab5401ec7dc","body":{"detail":"Connected::is_unconnected follows the filter's classes (spec §8.2, §5.2): a viewer comment with no public ID and a batch with no sender are Author::Unconnected, so their names get spec §9.6's suffix. On the golden fixture (crates/clax-server/tests/fixtures/single-owner-21.sql) the owner's two pre-migration-12 comments and one older batch now read 'Alex (not connected)' in comments_read, feedback and hook payloads; with §19's keys and the suffix removed the regenerated golden is identical. Options: keep (recommended: their author is unknown, and the *unconnected switch is what lets them reach agents, so the mark tells the truth); or exempt rows from before attribution from the mark while still filtering them as *unconnected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"31b72a09f53496f8d927466a9d2f661853a503a3fd7274e62dbae25d003fa4ac"},"summary":"Comments and batches from before authorship was recorded read '<name> (not connected)' to agents, the owner's own included","tags":["status:needs-decision","spec:9.6","spec:19","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:31.919166Z","id":"e8c8cb48967778f836e072ce40f7426cbac7f73f889241fd62f55b9a3f60d139","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"7fdbaaf50ad63d42fc3fd4a60db63c388e863bc07db94901a2863ab5401ec7dc","summary":"Review of 0d857bda: the 131 golden suffixes are 70 on LAN viewers (Mia 35, Viewer 35, legitimate under spec §19 item 7) and 61 on the owner's history: the two comments with author_public_id NULL and the send_batches row with no sender. No comment attributed to the owner row is marked. The class is wider than the fixture: comments the owner's browser made between migrations 12 and 15 carry a viewer row with minted_local NULL, which claim_for_owner (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs:596) never claims, so they also read '<name> (not connected)'. Recommended ruling: keep the mark (no unverified name reads as the owner's, §21.2; a pre-migration-12 LAN viewer could have used the owner's name) and amend §19 item 7 to list the owner's unattributed history (comments before migration 12, a browser identity never claimed for the owner, batches from before migration 25) as marked. Revisit: an owner-only, browser-only fold of a legacy viewer row into the owner from People would unmark the migration 12-15 class without trusting names.","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:31.919303Z","id":"1d3cb9483c89313efa58e04ef46b521eda0b4438174f09c440b5d78bbebb98ec","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:34c65221","summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-12): \"Keep the mark.\" Unattributed history (comments from before migration 12 or from a browser identity never claimed for the owner, and batches from before migration 25) reads '<name> (not connected)' to agents, the owner's own included. Spec §9.6 and §19 item 7 amended in 34c65221; golden_single_owner::the_golden_differs_only_as_section_19_lists passes with marks Alex 61, Mia 35, Viewer 35 and none on the owner's attributed comments.","supersedes":"7fdbaaf50ad63d42fc3fd4a60db63c388e863bc07db94901a2863ab5401ec7dc","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T00:21:31.923565Z","id":"b8541bcebcc46e53d57434f1bd2c3dcb4a5bfac87709b36a7794f41243e9e9d5","body":{"detail":"Unattributed history is marked '(not connected)' (owner's decision on 7fdbaaf5). Comments the owner's browser made between migrations 12 and 15 carry a viewer row with minted_local NULL that claim_for_owner (crates/clax-core/src/store/viewers.rs) never claims, so they are marked on real installs too. Matching names is spoofable (spec §21.2); an explicit fold by the owner in the browser is not.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"31b72a09f53496f8d927466a9d2f661853a503a3fd7274e62dbae25d003fa4ac"},"summary":"An owner-only, browser-only 'this was me' in People that folds a legacy viewer row (or claims unattributed comments) into the owner, unmarking that history without trusting names","tags":["revisit:owners report their own old comments marked as not connected","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:37:11.638714Z","id":"a2f5b46c2bf57af375dabd032ee171a399f0ccaf15d69ef97c48a516ebf1347d","body":{"detail":"A harness session ID that is itself ppid-123 or h followed by 32 hex characters is safe by the character rule, so its file is <harness>-ppid-123.json or <harness>-h<hex>.json, the same name as a parent-PID key or another ID's hashed key. Harness IDs are UUIDs today, so this is latent. write_private (lines 375-404) creates the directory 0700 only when it is missing; an existing remote-sessions directory with a wider mode is used as is (the files are still 0600).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":745},"end":{"line":766},"content_hash":"eacb5cdb3b148a813fe62ebaaf30d6a9f7e920feb321c77e4eb57bfc245d5011"},"suggested_fix":"Prefix the forms distinctly (for example <harness>-id-<id>.json, <harness>-h-<hex>.json, <harness>-ppid-<pid>.json, with the safe form refusing a leading id- / h- / ppid-), and set or check 0700 on an existing directory.","summary":"Credential file names can collide between a harness session ID and the hashed or parent-PID forms, and an existing remote-sessions directory keeps its mode","tags":["review","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:20.904133Z","id":"b323ca6a3723a73fa2c5aa665430634d192ea88f5a3a84737d9472a22881d45a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:903f2670","summary":"File names are <harness>-s-<id>, <harness>-h-<hash> and <harness>-p-<pid>, which never collide; the directory is set to 0700 when it exists; a directory or file that is a symbolic link is refused, not followed. Evidence: remote::session_file_tests::no_two_keys_share_a_file_name and the_directory_is_made_private_and_never_followed pass; the collision and kept-mode mutations are caught.","supersedes":"a2f5b46c2bf57af375dabd032ee171a399f0ccaf15d69ef97c48a516ebf1347d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:07:51.981925Z","id":"120442dab5137e748aada3cb1f48da8c1abeb1d8749c70ab4cf83071829e3bc1","body":{"detail":"process_started runs `ps -o lstart= -p <pid>` and SessionFiles::find (crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs, `same_process`) compares the string byte for byte with the one SessionFiles::write recorded. The text is local time in the locale: for one process, `Tue Oct 13 00:40:38 2026` as set, `Di. 13 Okt. 00:40:50 2026` with LC_TIME=de_DE.UTF-8 or LANG=de_DE.UTF-8, `Tue Oct 13 13:40:38 2026` with TZ=Asia/Tokyo. Codex's shim has no harness session ID, so its session is found only by codex-p-<pid>.json. Codex starts MCP servers with an allow-listed environment while hooks get the full one, so with LANG=en_US.UTF-8 and LC_TIME=de_DE.UTF-8 the shim records English text and the SessionStart hook computes German: the hook never takes the file, its join without proof matches the shim's row through the ancestor walk and is refused 401, it waits one second and fails, and every later hook fails with session_credential_missing. Hook first is no better: the shim's registration (no harness session ID, parent_pid = codex) matches the hook's row, cannot take the hook's file, and is refused after its last candidate. Where ps is missing (a slim Linux container), no -p- file is ever written or taken, with the same outcome; before this change the parent's own file needed no ps. The one-second resolution is not exploitable in practice (PIDs are allocated sequentially; a same-user attacker is inside waiver c4ff1520), but the same fix removes it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":776},"end":{"line":790},"content_hash":"b58fa3894bfc15fc304f21e4e1982fce14b2812a844d589fe704f74dad211987"},"suggested_fix":"Read the start time without ps: on macOS the libproc crate's pidinfo::<BSDInfo> (pbi_start_tvsec, pbi_start_tvusec; a safe API, its unsafe is outside Clax's crates), on Linux field 22 of /proc/<pid>/stat via std::fs; store it as a number. At minimum run ps with LC_ALL=C and TZ=UTC0 set on the Command. Add a test writing under one TZ or LANG and finding under another.","summary":"A parent-PID credential file's same-process check compares `ps -o lstart` text, which depends on ps being installed and on the locale and timezone, so Codex remote sessions fail where ps is missing or the shim's and hooks' LANG/LC_TIME/LC_ALL/TZ differ","tags":["review","spec:6.8","severity:important","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:07:51.982143Z","id":"d4ca7d364012301e4e54b331aca8bbdb3b91c47d722804fbfade5f19ef9073e9","body":{"detail":"SessionFiles::write always writes <harness>-p-<parent>.json for the row's parent PID. When one harness process holds two sessions whose rows share that parent (Codex /new, Claude Code /clear, a Codex app-server), the second session's SessionStart join (absorb in crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs) replaces the first row's file. A later Codex shim restart, which knows no harness session ID, takes the second row's credential and registers with parent_pid = <pid>; find_live matches either row, so the shim is either refused (401, then 401 with no credential: no session) or joins the other conversation's session. connect::a_nested_agents_hook_never_becomes_its_parents_session (crates/clax-cli/tests/connect.rs) shows the overwrite: both hooks share the test's PID, so C's join rewrites claude-p-<pid>.json with C's credential and C's SessionEnd removes it; the test asserts B's -s- file only. Separately, RemoteSession::forget for a SessionEnd input without session_id finds through the knows-none branch and removes an ancestor's -p- file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":983},"end":{"line":990},"content_hash":"1528f41a3bbd4c531e03470ffdc235d2d7fb774c33a37e9f75e05eecb0d5ce65"},"suggested_fix":"Leave a -p- file alone when it names another session that is still live, or key it by parent PID and row; make forget remove only files whose recorded harness_session_id is the hook's own.","summary":"Writing a row's parent-PID file replaces the file of another live row with the same parent process, and a SessionEnd hook with no session ID can delete an ancestor's file","tags":["review","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:07:51.982216Z","id":"5e74092505aeaccaef94ac592c67cff57561ad3afd6a893debf64f21650b77c6","body":{"detail":"read_file lstats the directory and the file, then std::fs::read(&path) follows symlinks; private_dir (crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs) lstats the directory, then set_permissions(&self.dir) follows one swapped in between. A FIFO at a credential name blocks std::fs::read, which hangs the shim's registration (no deadline; hooks are bounded by theirs). Only a same-user process can plant these, which is inside waiver c4ff1520; writes are safe (create_new, then rename).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":855},"end":{"line":884},"content_hash":"da34dc954489f51ea78d7c13de2fdebeedae7313a58db15465fc1f551a176c13"},"suggested_fix":"Open with OpenOptionsExt::custom_flags(libc::O_NOFOLLOW | libc::O_NONBLOCK), check the handle's metadata().is_file(), and read from the handle; open the directory and set its mode through the handle (File::set_permissions uses the descriptor). No unsafe is needed.","summary":"The credential files' symlink refusal is check-then-use (lstat, then a path-based read or chmod), and a non-regular file at a credential name blocks the reader","tags":["review","security","spec:6.8","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:51:49.480358Z","id":"263d57a7d55149c1ed83aa27aca6f15ab7f6284f5730a58411637d3a9909a1aa","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a8d0a534","summary":"process_started now returns microseconds since the epoch read from the kernel (macOS: libproc pidinfo BSDInfo pbi_start_tvsec/tvusec; Linux: /proc/<pid>/stat field 22 and btime), with `ps -o lstart=` under LC_ALL=C TZ=UTC0 parsed only elsewhere; the file stores the number (parent_started_us). Evidence: process_start_tests::a_processs_start_is_a_number_from_the_kernel_matching_ps_in_c_and_utc (agrees with ps in C/UTC to the second, while ps text in de_DE/Asia/Tokyo differs), ps_lstart_in_c_and_utc_parses_to_the_second, a_linux_start_is_the_boot_time_plus_field_22, and connect::a_codex_hook_finds_its_shims_session_by_its_parent_and_never_by_a_reused_pid, whose hook now runs with LANG, LC_TIME and LC_ALL de_DE.UTF-8 and TZ Asia/Tokyo, pass; the start-not-compared and Linux-field mutations are caught (target/t19a/mutations3.txt).","supersedes":"120442dab5137e748aada3cb1f48da8c1abeb1d8749c70ab4cf83071829e3bc1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:51:49.481324Z","id":"dbaf67733d6f0fe54b1f65f7817cb2d8221e8622c82e339c83f1ae9568e6d043","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a8d0a534","summary":"SessionFiles::write keeps a parent-PID file that holds another session of the same process (replacing it only for its own session or for a file written for an earlier process with that PID), and a hook that knows no harness session ID removes no files at its end. Evidence: session_file_tests_2::a_parent_pid_file_of_another_session_of_the_same_process_is_kept, hook::remote_session_tests::a_hook_forgets_only_its_own_rows_files, and connect::a_nested_agents_hook_never_becomes_its_parents_session (now asserting B's -p- file survives C's join and C's end) pass; the replace and forget-without-session-ID mutations are caught (target/t19a/mutations3.txt, mutations3b.txt).","supersedes":"d4ca7d364012301e4e54b331aca8bbdb3b91c47d722804fbfade5f19ef9073e9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:51:49.482087Z","id":"647d4eea008c14008939dae429f671bb246b2d15c17432cdbf3a76d6cbd66af7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a8d0a534","summary":"Credential files are opened with openat on the directory's own handle (opened O_NOFOLLOW|O_DIRECTORY) with O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK, checked to be regular files on the handle, read through it (capped at 64 KiB); the directory's mode is set through its handle; writes use openat O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW then renameat. Evidence: session_file_tests_2::a_file_that_is_not_a_regular_file_is_refused_without_blocking (a FIFO is refused at once) and session_file_tests::the_directory_is_made_private_and_never_followed pass; the follow-links, any-file-type and dir-mode mutations are caught (target/t19a/mutations3.txt).","supersedes":"5e74092505aeaccaef94ac592c67cff57561ad3afd6a893debf64f21650b77c6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:26.297849Z","id":"cabd862f6f06b0711e94fa17ae0da0390d7f444b66a0c8528ffe9751d7f34f00","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"263d57a7d55149c1ed83aa27aca6f15ab7f6284f5730a58411637d3a9909a1aa","summary":"Since ef51c6d9 the start comes from sysinfo (default features off, system only) on macOS and Linux, to the second, stored as parent_started_s; libproc and its build-time bindgen are gone. process_start_tests::a_processs_start_is_a_number_from_the_kernel_matching_ps_in_c_and_utc (equal to ps in C/UTC, while ps text in de_DE/Asia/Tokyo differs) and connect::a_codex_hook_finds_its_shims_session_by_its_parent_and_never_by_a_reused_pid (hook under de_DE locale and Tokyo time zone) pass.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/names.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.715500Z","id":"8bb1f335a7a8fbe9df4c3d78e211f74acbee86aea131a4417351a8a7f26a55ff","body":{"detail":"The row keeps only its name and name_source `derived`, not the repository its name came from, so derive(Some(\"codex\"), None, \"codex\") = \"codex\" passes named_after_harness(\"codex\", \"codex\"). The join and registration in crates/clax-core/src/store/sessions.rs:624 and :819 then rename it after the new repository, so `@codex` stops resolving. Rare, since it needs the repository to be named after the harness.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":80},"end":{"line":86},"content_hash":"343cabfd43501130566489a8b611b25a338c8771a117833eeaf87a022e604517"},"suggested_fix":"Record the harness-only origin on the row (a name_source of its own, or the repository the name was derived from) and rename only that.","summary":"named_after_harness cannot tell a harness-only name from a repository name of the same form: a Codex session in a repository named `codex` (or a Claude session in `claude`, or repository `claude` on branch `2`) is still renamed when it joins from another repository","tags":["review","names","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/clips.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:16:36.718062Z","id":"10863fd6b435009ac4d3c41d2b4f8ae47b425e2c9c719f8cfeada9dbe251753e","body":{"detail":"The threads cannot hold the hook open: run() ends with std::process::exit(0) (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs:778), and a held clip request through a proxy was verified to leave the hook exiting at about 3.9 s. The thread count follows the number of distinct clips the daemon hands over, and write_private (crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs:375) removes its temporary file only on an error it sees, not on exit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":71},"end":{"line":107},"content_hash":"89e5b29f6a249845a889b714192f438f9b583a516b36339e217c5ef8427c0e9c"},"suggested_fix":"Fetch at most a few clips at once, and sweep `.*.tmp` files older than a minute from the clip cache when storing.","summary":"fetch_within spawns one thread per distinct clip with no limit, and the hook's fetch builds two blocking reqwest clients (each with its own runtime thread) on each; a thread still writing when the hook calls std::process::exit leaves a .tmp file in remote-cache/clips","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:13:53.804309Z","id":"1fc0d7a04502ca3e21703d5939517685ad6308a9b60674e8aaafb3423ed9f784","body":{"detail":"cap_raise drops from a raise only the actions a narrowing allows nowhere (and lowers db levels). A narrowing that allows an action at some artifacts only (made outside People, which narrows by whole actions: see the concern on web/shell/src/people/model.ts about whole actions) leaves that action on for a raise at any other artifact. Capping by location would cancel every raise at another person's artifact, because a narrowing is stated within the person's rights (Collaborator's update is at own), so the spec (§7.2) chose action and level; a narrowing that names artifacts would need its locations read as 'turned off elsewhere' to cap by place.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":754},"end":{"line":782},"content_hash":"bc434e4b793e424ca7b0c5d365ddd0bc580f61c5471491789526920668cbb6db"},"summary":"A narrowing caps a raise by action and db level, never by location","tags":["spec:7.2","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T04:47:17.410845Z","id":"6b9774cfa58a3bfc640cffcd6309d4f8f4633687677a23bca35b9f6e28b38c2f","body":{"detail":"The owner's selection, verbatim: \"Remove is enough\": narrowing caps raises only for actions the person holds; for anything else they use Remove; People's narrowing panel stays as it is. cap_raise is confirmed as built; spec §7.2 says so.","kind":"comment","references":"1fc0d7a04502ca3e21703d5939517685ad6308a9b60674e8aaafb3423ed9f784","summary":"Decided (owner, 2026-10-14): \"Remove is enough\": capping by action and level, never by location, stands","tags":["status:decided","owner-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:07:02.775279Z","id":"1d727e67a24cfaf3b6a859467ec55a3dc784a33158139d1af6eff3079cb2369a","body":{"detail":"withheld_comments_line formats `[clax] {n} comments from {author} on {title} (thread {id}) are withheld until your person approves them.` for every n (its test at crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:2272 pins `1 comments`). Spec section 8.3 gives the template with `N comments ... are`; section 3.3 step 3 shows `1 comment from Mia ... is withheld`. The feedback header elsewhere says `1 comment` (docs/contract.md 'Payload').","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":792},"end":{"line":792},"content_hash":"cb67cf529b2da1e141dd55ea99026613e913ee5d1121afe0cec959b39ccb91ef"},"summary":"The withheld-comments line reads '1 comments ... are withheld' for one comment, where spec section 3.3's example reads '1 comment ... is withheld'","tags":["task:24","people","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:29.991352Z","id":"00d296290500643e92e70efb627030d1fc8947cf3567ba96a6556e7fc149a09a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f0303f18","summary":"Fixed: withheld_comments_line reads '1 comment ... is withheld until your person approves it' for one comment. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-core -E 'test(placeholders_replace_fields_and_keep_the_object)' passes with the singular case pinned; api_visibility::a_revocation_during_a_wait_withholds_what_follows_it and api_people tests assert '1 comment from'; workspace nextest 2256 passed.","supersedes":"1d727e67a24cfaf3b6a859467ec55a3dc784a33158139d1af6eff3079cb2369a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T04:35:36.735976Z","id":"45678e7378f4bbcb38edf1bac7577fc82a3f2935f741fdba727162fe5e393eb6","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"00d296290500643e92e70efb627030d1fc8947cf3567ba96a6556e7fc149a09a","summary":"Correction to the evidence: the server test that asserts the singular line is api_visibility::revocation_during_wait_for_feedback_holds_rows (crates/clax-server/tests/api_visibility.rs:2563), not the name given above.","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox": "1", "type": "annotation", "subject": "crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs", "issuer": "mailto:kesling@empathic.dev", "issuer_type": "ai", "created_at": "2026-10-15T22:16:41.500714Z", "body": {"kind": "concern", "summary": "A connected person's clax_viewer cookie is the viewer row's monotonic ULID (new_ulid), not an unguessable secret", "detail": "redeem_browser_code (store/people.rs:754) sets clax_viewer to the person row's id, minted by new_ulid() (ids.rs:70) at invite time (people.rs:835) or grant-approve (people.rs:1244). new_ulid is one process-global generator whose within-ms values are a per-ms random base incremented by one; the same generator mints viewer rows for any anonymous LAN peer via GET /api/viewers/me (routes/viewers.rs:34). So same-ms ids are consecutive integers and a foreign person-row mint is an enumerable hole in an attacker's observed run. Reproduced: cookie = invite_id-1; GET /api/people/me, /api/inbox, /api/approvals returned Eve's data over the LAN, and POST /api/approvals/requests/<id>/decide passed the SameOrigin+person gate (404 not 403). No rate limit on /api/people/me. The branch newly binds person identity/inbox/approval authority to this value; S21.4 accepts only sniffing, not prediction. Important rather than Critical because the attacker must mint during the ~1ms unobservable invite-creation window (grant-approve mints the connecting party's own cookie, no third-party gain).", "suggested_fix": "Mint the clax_viewer cookie value from a CSPRNG independent of the row id (e.g. redeem_browser_code stores viewers.cookie_sha256 and looks it up by hash), or draw viewer/person row ids from a non-monotonic random source, so a person's browser credential has real 80-bit+ entropy.", "span": {"start": {"line": 70}, "end": {"line": 81}}, "tags": ["review", "final-review", "rights", "security", "session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}, "id": "5cb671424df63f5f9097ef72cf2f044278378381c3c8be8691ecf7444c4e6ae1"}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.648040Z","id":"ec1fe619d797a4813d18f1a1afebccb5aff10c46d7e826df5159cdb5ee6aaaa3","body":{"detail":"Files are removed only by the shim's exit, the SessionEnd hook and clax connect --off; a harness killed hard leaves <harness>-s-<id>.json and <harness>-p-<pid>.json behind, and a parent-PID file of a dead process is never reused unless the PID comes back. After the review's runs one home held ten such files. They are refused when presented (the secret is cleared), so this is clutter, not exposure of a live session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1157},"end":{"line":1168},"content_hash":"3d026df08888088edb4b711a05b95db10838edd505e66b828e6ebf2dc43ca034"},"suggested_fix":"When a registration or join is refused for a file's credential, or on the shim's start, remove files whose parent PID no longer names the recorded process.","summary":"Credential files of sessions whose shim or hook never ran its cleanup stay in remote-sessions/ indefinitely","tags":["review","remote","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T22:16:49.648137Z","id":"79273f8168d4c39a5573de11feab8115c08756f481275a350bef7010fa36698b","body":{"detail":"A shim started before --off keeps its grant in memory; its next call is grant_revoked, worded 'this machine was disconnected from <url>: run `clax connect --off`, then connect again with a new invite'. Reproduced. The first half is already done, and remote.json is gone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":682},"end":{"line":692},"content_hash":"70cf6d77c24df40067df989d7f28d1459c8a7699cd0abd1e76247efd3929ad2c"},"suggested_fix":"Word it so it reads right whether or not remote.json still exists (e.g. 'connect again with a new invite (clax connect --off first if remote.json remains)').","summary":"After `clax connect --off`, an agent still running there is told to run `clax connect --off`","tags":["review","remote","final-review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.131059Z","id":"cfc2f5735d2ec9403295d5b3f2a050324e6af3ff8264796dcd31dcac0a7fc3df","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:09a93977","summary":"Fixed in 09a93977: clax_viewer cookies are cxv_ secrets of 32 random bytes (clax_core::secret::viewer_cookie) minted at browser-link redemption and per new anonymous viewer, kept as SHA-256 in viewer_cookies and looked up by hash, never by row ID; legacy row-ID cookies from main never name a person and are replaced at GET /api/viewers/me. Evidence: cargo nextest run -p clax-server --test integration -E 'test(/a_persons_cookie_is_a_secret_that_no_row_id_reaches|an_anonymous_viewers_cookie_is_a_secret_not_its_row_id|a_legacy_viewer_cookie_is_replaced_and_never_names_a_person/)' -> 3 passed (api_people.rs: invite-ID and person-ID neighbours +-1, +-2 answer as no cookie does).","supersedes":"5cb671424df63f5f9097ef72cf2f044278378381c3c8be8691ecf7444c4e6ae1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.152334Z","id":"cd753441fbe303a79381f044c90bec1ec8b8db87e46903eb15926172c47deb90","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c5f95b5b","summary":"Fixed in c5f95b5b: SessionFiles::write prunes parent-PID files of gone processes and files unused for STALE_FILE_AFTER (7 days); the shim's heartbeat and Pi's tool-call reports mark their files in use (touch). Evidence: remote::tests::writing_a_credential_prunes_the_files_no_session_will_use passes; Pi 'marks its own credential file in use' passes.","supersedes":"ec1fe619d797a4813d18f1a1afebccb5aff10c46d7e826df5159cdb5ee6aaaa3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:10:27.154707Z","id":"f0ae6f154de9ce4a0f13ca59aa46ffc08d76c42e1ef690cc09d69029d082d336","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c5f95b5b","summary":"Fixed in c5f95b5b: refusal_message checks whether the signer's remote.json still exists; after --off it says to connect again with a new invite, not to run --off. Evidence: remote::tests::grant_revoked_asks_for_connect_off_only_while_the_connection_is_on_file passes.","supersedes":"79273f8168d4c39a5573de11feab8115c08756f481275a350bef7010fa36698b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T06:32:05.305819Z","id":"9ae7436059a1bbc5e990c52282b19336b0a885e3f79da589b4986e82d75d5574","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cbca495ec17bb7b2d7d70077d1b1b1dbb113fdb3","summary":"Moved to crates/clax-core/src/store/visibility.rs:72:79 as 1ce70140 in git:cbca495e","supersedes":"b8541bcebcc46e53d57434f1bd2c3dcb4a5bfac87709b36a7794f41243e9e9d5","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:38:27.016814Z","id":"511784cdf43052bc5879ea8065430da5aa0a753efd64bec0b8d013685fbce1ab","body":{"detail":"Seats::take ORs the claim's reserved flag into the held seat and nothing clears it, so a person whose rights stop naming the artifact keeps a seat outside the pool until their last connection leaves or the seat goes idle; for that time the artifact seats one more person than SeatLimits::people. A share granted while seated is the mirror case: the seat stays counted against the pool until it is taken again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":355},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"22b83b7cb0b7e3c4447991cdead0cce6229e630f9bbe0057d502a7ef02616cd1"},"summary":"A seat taken as reserved stays reserved after the share that named the artifact is revoked","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:04:49.653337Z","id":"dded3e3c5a75314f88ac7e9a501dd7be1311fc3dd414d17d7456ab41b3bf602a","body":{"detail":"MAX_SESSION_DRAFTS (8) keeps one session from holding every one of MAX_LIVE_DRAFTS (64), but an agent with the daemon token or a grant registers sessions freely, so eight sessions of one agent on 64 artifacts refuse every other draft (429 limit_reached) for as long as they revise every DRAFT_IDLE_SECS. A per-person or per-credential cap would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":270},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"c033bab2d06989d00619b09e2a15c9573daed827b613027117bf9fda8214a68e"},"summary":"Eight sessions still fill the 64 live drafts: session registration is not limited","tags":["drafts","limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:02.671084Z","id":"3677015b0375e19e8135ae33ed1ed3d027567262f11c0b87eab784403f6a93a2","body":{"detail":"Spec §16.5 ranks first the people in the thread the receiver has open by what they have open, type in or wrote there. in_thread() counts having it open, typing and drafting there, not having written a comment in it: the relay keeps no store access, and the hosted prototype (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts flushLive) reads thread authors with a query per flush. A caller could pass the open thread's author set to Relay::batches if the cap of 30 is ever reached with a thread's past writers left out.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":364},"content_hash":"3be9a58b426f018c42c9cae61b1f12edd9a740de2a9ab7ea57470f1d15cf9dd4"},"summary":"Ranking leaves out the people who wrote in the receiver's open thread","tags":["live-layers","revisit:an artifact has more than 30 people showing live state at once","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:23:02.671251Z","id":"5d0971fb5e3cb7158aeb448b55d75ab99e576193906ebc7cb0b9a8419baa1022","body":{"detail":"thread_ok() takes any ULID: checking that it names one of the artifact's threads would cost a store read per typing or draft message (up to 30 a second per socket). A draft on a thread that is not the artifact's reaches receivers, whose sidebar shows drafts only on threads it lists (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte passes writers(t.id) per card), so it is never shown; the cost is the relayed bytes, bounded by the token bucket and MAX_DRAFT_CHARS.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"2363a35975ff383585b9cc0d721c441f0b83475b1b5a800af6ee54fc7e3cb305"},"summary":"A live message's thread ID is checked for shape only, not as a thread of the artifact","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.912577Z","id":"84e34b90ce8107f83e644be174565d013967d16ac17a81135194eb89f4cd34f7","body":{"detail":"A receiver's shell shows writers only through writersIn(layer, t.id) for the cards of its own artifact's threads and writersIn(layer, null) for new comments (web/shell/src/ui/Sidebar.svelte, web/shell/src/ui/ShellSidebar.svelte); thread IDs are ULIDs, so another artifact's thread is never one of those cards, and every viewer of an artifact sees all of its threads (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs: the filter is for agent channels only). The sender learns nothing back: its own state is never echoed (Relay::batches skips the receiver's person; tests a_receiver_gets_others_but_never_itself and api_live_layers::a_persons_pointer_typing_and_draft_reach_the_others), and ranking by a receiver's open thread changes only what that receiver gets. What a foreign ID costs is its bytes to each receiver, bounded by the token bucket and MAX_DRAFT_CHARS. A hosted port where people see only some of an artifact's threads would need the check this waiver forgoes.","kind":"comment","references":"5d0971fb5e3cb7158aeb448b55d75ab99e576193906ebc7cb0b9a8419baa1022","span":{"start":{"line":172},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"2363a35975ff383585b9cc0d721c441f0b83475b1b5a800af6ee54fc7e3cb305"},"summary":"Checked: a foreign thread ID neither shows a draft where it should not nor reveals a thread","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:01.912681Z","id":"a779cdaaa995d09e0beee81ba31cfa3d7c7884c046a611167334934657f18cba","body":{"detail":"One person with several tabs is one sender, owned by the socket that wrote last; leave() removes the whole state when that socket closes, so a draft typed in another still-open tab disappears for everyone until that tab sends again (web/shell/src/view/live-layers.ts DraftSender sends again only on its next input or on a reconnect). Nothing leaks; others just stop seeing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":492},"end":{"line":498},"content_hash":"5ba0242afc679c47676d5405c347cd6707bac11ecb9fcda30084aacf1bf382a5"},"suggested_fix":"Keep each sender's parts per socket and show the latest of the person's open sockets, or have leave() hand the state to the person's other socket instead of removing it.","summary":"Closing the tab that wrote last drops a person's live state while another tab of theirs is still open","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:12:31.534539Z","id":"bdf2cf97626c8fd94bc55e5e6cc98d926e035e8cf22527b15eab9da13d3662a7","body":{"detail":"render_item knows a clip only through FeedbackItem::clip_path, which since 274f3832 is local_clip's path and so None for a Durable Object's or MemContent's clips; the item has no has_clip field, so a thread that has a clip reads to the agent as having none. The clip is served at /api/artifacts/<id>/threads/<tid>/clip either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":300},"end":{"line":306},"content_hash":"19810dbf3470273b3a5067c609135f38ac1bd433c4963d9cc05379d7e2aebb02"},"suggested_fix":"Carry has_clip (or the clip URL) on FeedbackItem and render 'Clip: at <url>' when there is no local file.","summary":"A clip kept in a content store with no local files renders as 'Clip: none (no screenshot was captured for this comment)'","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:53:18.948186Z","id":"54ac59bced39bbd2b746a9d94180180cf0e9729d57af1a38fd06c7cbf3a3b2f9","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":141},"content_hash":"bce38f8db344254aa9b58017056a5819d49c6dd0366968b8fb1739351d29343f"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T09:54:20.993717Z","id":"d910e3a59d8bf26ab25dd791f3339705de2caae165d3c435e50d831a29a5e1ac","body":{"detail":"Seats::take ORs the claim's reserved flag into the held seat and nothing clears it, so a person whose rights stop naming the artifact keeps a seat outside the pool until their last connection leaves or the seat goes idle; for that time the artifact seats one more person than SeatLimits::people. A share granted while seated is the mirror case: the seat stays counted against the pool until it is taken again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":380},"end":{"line":380},"content_hash":"22b83b7cb0b7e3c4447991cdead0cce6229e630f9bbe0057d502a7ef02616cd1"},"summary":"A seat taken as reserved stays reserved after the share that named the artifact is revoked","supersedes":"511784cdf43052bc5879ea8065430da5aa0a753efd64bec0b8d013685fbce1ab","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T12:12:33.138996Z","id":"bea2c1a7e0244cb5348cf9b7fd24e6a24ece24796a5e7cee2fbb8f0e0462c5c1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3677015b0375e19e8135ae33ed1ed3d027567262f11c0b87eab784403f6a93a2","summary":"The hosted/ files this record cites were removed in 60298c1d (the TypeScript prototype's retirement); read one at its parent with git show 60298c1d^:hosted/<path>","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372345Z","id":"129e50ba45d4ae89697a76abc8fca5cf9403e66792a3519043f7d4779bfcbfb8","body":{"detail":"MAX_LIVE_DRAFTS (64) times MAX_DRAFT_BYTES (1 MiB) are the daemon's limits, unchanged on wasm32, where the instance object shares 128 MB with every object in its isolate. One person with eight agent tokens (MAX_SESSION_DRAFTS 8 each) can fill them all.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"9be27a32dbf5cdd28f58b17c9ce9c15fb84ccb7170b5f171c080a08e45d07e91"},"suggested_fix":"A smaller total on wasm32 (for example 16 live drafts) or a byte budget across live drafts.","summary":"Live drafts may hold 64 MiB on the Worker, half an isolate","tags":["worker","resource","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"6ded859508ff599fa0ec068eff3d15b88cc7e9e53cc234056472a772d6a1105f","body":{"detail":"render_item knows a clip only through FeedbackItem::clip_path, which since 274f3832 is local_clip's path and so None for a Durable Object's or MemContent's clips; the item has no has_clip field, so a thread that has a clip reads to the agent as having none. The clip is served at /api/artifacts/<id>/threads/<tid>/clip either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"19810dbf3470273b3a5067c609135f38ac1bd433c4963d9cc05379d7e2aebb02"},"suggested_fix":"Carry has_clip (or the clip URL) on FeedbackItem and render 'Clip: at <url>' when there is no local file.","summary":"A clip kept in a content store with no local files renders as 'Clip: none (no screenshot was captured for this comment)'","supersedes":"bdf2cf97626c8fd94bc55e5e6cc98d926e035e8cf22527b15eab9da13d3662a7","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/live_layers.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"7c2027b222d0a7b4dcb671a983e3fd7b8ac732728c0fd46d9f02809fc1e21a90","body":{"detail":"One person with several tabs is one sender, owned by the socket that wrote last; leave() removes the whole state when that socket closes, so a draft typed in another still-open tab disappears for everyone until that tab sends again (web/shell/src/view/live-layers.ts DraftSender sends again only on its next input or on a reconnect). Nothing leaks; others just stop seeing it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":495},"end":{"line":501},"content_hash":"5ba0242afc679c47676d5405c347cd6707bac11ecb9fcda30084aacf1bf382a5"},"suggested_fix":"Keep each sender's parts per socket and show the latest of the person's open sockets, or have leave() hand the state to the person's other socket instead of removing it.","summary":"Closing the tab that wrote last drops a person's live state while another tab of theirs is still open","supersedes":"a779cdaaa995d09e0beee81ba31cfa3d7c7884c046a611167334934657f18cba","tags":["live-layers","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T19:07:12.535250Z","id":"2ff392bdaf73205b4b1c21dcbcea3156a189438d81b604705bf4d96836fc5fe0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6ded859508ff599fa0ec068eff3d15b88cc7e9e53cc234056472a772d6a1105f","summary":"For an agent token's session on a hosted Clax the item now carries the clip at its keyed address (FeedbackItem::clip, set by link_clips in crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs) and renders 'Clip: <url> (<note>)'. A daemon-token or other non-grant session on a content store with no local files still reads 'none (no screenshot was captured ...)'.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/clips.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:21.748573Z","id":"c53eb43e764a03cc671d4e7c949aaccc20973a98ad99f519bfc2ab8ea85318cd","body":{"detail":"The threads cannot hold the hook open: run() ends with std::process::exit(0) (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/hook.rs:778), and a held clip request through a proxy was verified to leave the hook exiting at about 3.9 s. The thread count follows the number of distinct clips the daemon hands over, and write_private (crates/clax-core/src/remote.rs:375) removes its temporary file only on an error it sees, not on exit.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":113},"content_hash":"89e5b29f6a249845a889b714192f438f9b583a516b36339e217c5ef8427c0e9c"},"suggested_fix":"Fetch at most a few clips at once, and sweep `.*.tmp` files older than a minute from the clip cache when storing.","summary":"fetch_within spawns one thread per distinct clip with no limit, and the hook's fetch builds two blocking reqwest clients (each with its own runtime thread) on each; a thread still writing when the hook calls std::process::exit leaves a .tmp file in remote-cache/clips","supersedes":"10863fd6b435009ac4d3c41d2b4f8ae47b425e2c9c719f8cfeada9dbe251753e","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:52:20.536854Z","id":"fad4f4b6e699693cae00be7f5822cefe848579b371bdfe4baaeaa0534ee7fb19","body":{"detail":"clax_core::content stays in clax-core: it is a trait and two implementations with no SQLite, implemented again by clax-content-git and crates/clax-worker, which would otherwise depend on clax-store and link rusqlite for it. The layout spec (section 2.1) names clax-store 'the SQLite store'; content is the files beside it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":13},"content_hash":"a19f42794e98e4b4ae69b98d2c2d12f03da6b0c5668d5006647ab7a845a08990"},"summary":"Move the ContentStore trait and its fs and memory stores into clax-store","tags":["layout","revisit:a content store implementation needs the store's tables","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:52:24.267917Z","id":"e77ac38e07033c6dc3aa1cc80e4dd999108c1f2a7807c067605139fff77e17ab","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §1 says a hidden or unfocused tab never counts as Clax attention. `Signals.clax_at` (surface.rs:76-79) instead takes `Presence::engaged_at` (crates/clax-core/src/presence.rs), which returns a live tab's last input time even when the tab is unfocused, plus the report time of a focused tab. The reading taken: an input is a dated event the spec lists apart from focus (§1 'the person's last input on the page'), so it counts; what never counts is the tab's hidden or unfocused state by itself. The strict reading would drop the input of any tab not focused at its last report, so a person who typed in Clax a moment ago and then switched to the terminal would show no Clax signal at all.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":76},"end":{"line":79},"content_hash":"cc77a9c6c5a7f3842c3884947fe901644d20e7fad8510d121c519a2b670ff71a"},"summary":"Count only tabs focused at their last report as Clax engagement, not an unfocused tab's last input","tags":["revisit:a person reports being asked in Clax right after switching away from a tab they had just typed in","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:52:24.268017Z","id":"522ad2d2ecd56bbadde592da9a08e3c638d3dd7294b36452d2322bbf3f349448","body":{"detail":"Spec §1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md) lists 'the only signal is an inferred terminal turn (Codex, Grok)' as unsure. `suggest` reads 'only' literally: an inferred turn gives Clax, unsure (surface.rs:167-174) only when no Clax signal (tab input, focused report or delivery) exists at all; an inferred turn newer than the newest Clax signal by TIE_SECS or more gives Terminal, clear (surface.rs:175-193), exactly as a typed prompt would, and within TIE_SECS it is a tie (Clax, unsure). The other reading would make every inferred turn at most unsure (Terminal, unsure or Clax, unsure), on the grounds that a turn without a prompt hook may be an agent's own continuation rather than the person typing. Covered by surface::tests::an_inferred_turn_alone_is_unsure. Needs the owner to confirm which reading the spec means.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":165},"end":{"line":193},"content_hash":"8398c9000061b3b7d79426e61531db01bb23e0428b1eb4890896d6e76929cc65"},"summary":"Never let an inferred terminal turn give a clear terminal suggestion","tags":["revisit:a Codex, Grok or Pi session is suggested the terminal (clear) while its person was in Clax","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:52:24.268057Z","id":"345592512a189adf4774b782a2d5ea2ca42abb4da80a7f448f14f08913705e66","body":{"detail":"`suggest` returns Terminal, clear whenever `Signals.clax_open` is false (surface.rs:118-124), before any other rule, because Clax cannot show a question to a person with no Clax tab or extension panel open. Spec §1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md) says no signal in five minutes is unsure and that unsure leans to Clax; a strict reading would give Clax, unsure for a quiet session even with nothing open, so the question waits in the inbox for the person's next visit. Covered by surface::tests::with_no_clax_open_the_terminal_is_clear_whatever_else.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":118},"end":{"line":124},"content_hash":"1b838d621cc6e213eaa420567c1352a1df0b48327086ad12658bc02f4fe157f9"},"summary":"With no Clax tab or panel open, apply spec §1's unsure rule instead of a clear terminal","tags":["revisit:people want questions from a quiet session left in the Clax inbox rather than asked in the terminal when no Clax tab is open","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:05:14.008835Z","id":"78fb4a00e78b2e611b8ef15e193141cb1b36898d58bc03df09e238226222ed6c","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §1 says a hidden or unfocused tab never counts as Clax attention. `Signals.clax_at` (surface.rs:77-80) instead takes `Presence::engaged_at` (crates/clax-core/src/presence.rs), which returns a live tab's last input time even when the tab is unfocused, plus the report time of a focused tab. The reading taken: an input is a dated event the spec lists apart from focus (§1 'the person's last input on the page'), so it counts; what never counts is the tab's hidden or unfocused state by itself. The strict reading would drop the input of any tab not focused at its last report, so a person who typed in Clax a moment ago and then switched to the terminal would show no Clax signal at all.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":77},"end":{"line":80},"content_hash":"cc77a9c6c5a7f3842c3884947fe901644d20e7fad8510d121c519a2b670ff71a"},"summary":"Count only tabs focused at their last report as Clax engagement, not an unfocused tab's last input","supersedes":"e77ac38e07033c6dc3aa1cc80e4dd999108c1f2a7807c067605139fff77e17ab","tags":["revisit:a person reports being asked in Clax right after switching away from a tab they had just typed in","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:05:14.057570Z","id":"cede921d518734492f67058bc2ad66623a335a7c0b8473d5c2bdddeb92e5176a","body":{"detail":"Spec §1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md) lists 'the only signal is an inferred terminal turn (Codex, Grok)' as unsure. `suggest` reads 'only' literally: an inferred turn gives Clax, unsure (surface.rs:171-178) only when no Clax signal (tab input, focused report or delivery) exists at all; an inferred turn newer than the newest Clax signal by TIE_SECS or more gives Terminal, clear (surface.rs:179-206), exactly as a typed prompt would, and within TIE_SECS it is a tie (Clax, unsure). The other reading would make every inferred turn at most unsure (Terminal, unsure or Clax, unsure), on the grounds that a turn without a prompt hook may be an agent's own continuation rather than the person typing. Covered by surface::tests::an_inferred_turn_alone_is_unsure. Needs the owner to confirm which reading the spec means.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"9007ea6a999e51dd88e51945b3d38f655b0ff1fe289ec75abad44756a3ce98cf"},"summary":"Never let an inferred terminal turn give a clear terminal suggestion","supersedes":"522ad2d2ecd56bbadde592da9a08e3c638d3dd7294b36452d2322bbf3f349448","tags":["revisit:a Codex, Grok or Pi session is suggested the terminal (clear) while its person was in Clax","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:05:14.133971Z","id":"5b8cb5a05be3de95421b44adad711c80c42858713cfbf08610dff26da885e5de","body":{"detail":"`suggest` returns Terminal, clear whenever `Signals.clax_open` is false (surface.rs:121-128), before any other rule, because Clax cannot show a question to a person with no Clax tab or extension panel open. Spec §1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md) says no signal in five minutes is unsure and that unsure leans to Clax; a strict reading would give Clax, unsure for a quiet session even with nothing open, so the question waits in the inbox for the person's next visit. Covered by surface::tests::with_no_clax_open_the_terminal_is_clear_whatever_else.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"093c21531e52a1086533dd239d1fc482aa9ade1f34e4b0c723aaea28c8c3dae6"},"summary":"With no Clax tab or panel open, apply spec §1's unsure rule instead of a clear terminal","supersedes":"345592512a189adf4774b782a2d5ea2ca42abb4da80a7f448f14f08913705e66","tags":["revisit:people want questions from a quiet session left in the Clax inbox rather than asked in the terminal when no Clax tab is open","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:05:22.961643Z","id":"d5fc0c930a5a1a1c599e143934854e3f95f8defc8942df49f63a94ca7ae69279","body":{"detail":"In suggest (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs:171-206) the Clax side is the newest of Signals.clax_at and the delivery's time, with no age limit. With no Clax signal at all, an inferred turn 5 s ago gives Clax, unsure (surface.rs:171-178); add a Clax input from an hour ago and the same turn gives Terminal, clear (surface.rs:179-206). An option for the owner: count only Clax signals within QUIET_SECS when deciding whether the inferred turn is the only signal, so a stale Clax signal leaves the turn unsure.","kind":"comment","references":"cede921d518734492f67058bc2ad66623a335a7c0b8473d5c2bdddeb92e5176a","summary":"The reading has an asymmetry: a Clax signal of any age turns an inferred turn from unsure to Terminal, clear","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.261003Z","id":"143e782bffed945793df8052b556fae170e668f5c91d7dfd1067d08f49a1640b","body":{"detail":"Since Store::note_answer (crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs) records an answered or pulled question's time as Delivery.written_at, suggest's 'wrote' wording describes an act that was not writing in a thread. The agent reads the why to override the suggestion, so it is slightly misleading; the surface and confidence are right.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":171},"end":{"line":180},"content_hash":"e982dc592d1f9e7d987bca67e5ab157922a58ccc69357d5c8b47998aa96be127"},"suggested_fix":"Carry what the person did in Delivery (wrote, answered, pulled) and name it in the why, e.g. 'the person answered your question in Clax N s ago'.","summary":"The why for a delivery's activity says 'the person wrote in the delivered thread', also for an answer, a skip or Ask me here","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.354312Z","id":"334ba3a51d94ae251f4ab9ec00f36b8b22a1c8ec781a17577a76c8242a1d9685","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md §1 says a hidden or unfocused tab never counts as Clax attention. `Signals.clax_at` (surface.rs:129-132) instead takes `Presence::engaged_at` (crates/clax-core/src/presence.rs), which returns a live tab's last input time even when the tab is unfocused, plus the report time of a focused tab. The reading taken: an input is a dated event the spec lists apart from focus (§1 'the person's last input on the page'), so it counts; what never counts is the tab's hidden or unfocused state by itself. The strict reading would drop the input of any tab not focused at its last report, so a person who typed in Clax a moment ago and then switched to the terminal would show no Clax signal at all.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":129},"end":{"line":132},"content_hash":"cc77a9c6c5a7f3842c3884947fe901644d20e7fad8510d121c519a2b670ff71a"},"summary":"Count only tabs focused at their last report as Clax engagement, not an unfocused tab's last input","supersedes":"78fb4a00e78b2e611b8ef15e193141cb1b36898d58bc03df09e238226222ed6c","tags":["revisit:a person reports being asked in Clax right after switching away from a tab they had just typed in","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.378121Z","id":"486ead0e1b5fadfe0967e0c4b3a93862649efabbf71baf51f0b60a8da1671ae9","body":{"detail":"`suggest` returns Terminal, clear whenever `Signals.clax_open` is false (surface.rs:176-183), before any other rule, because Clax cannot show a question to a person with no Clax tab or extension panel open. Spec §1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md) says no signal in five minutes is unsure and that unsure leans to Clax; a strict reading would give Clax, unsure for a quiet session even with nothing open, so the question waits in the inbox for the person's next visit. Covered by surface::tests::with_no_clax_open_the_terminal_is_clear_whatever_else.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":176},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"093c21531e52a1086533dd239d1fc482aa9ade1f34e4b0c723aaea28c8c3dae6"},"summary":"With no Clax tab or panel open, apply spec §1's unsure rule instead of a clear terminal","supersedes":"5b8cb5a05be3de95421b44adad711c80c42858713cfbf08610dff26da885e5de","tags":["revisit:people want questions from a quiet session left in the Clax inbox rather than asked in the terminal when no Clax tab is open","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.401230Z","id":"8ccc53cd496662b83fc1d8f745d0d65c0ea8869651b353898812f34666eee5ca","body":{"detail":"Spec §1 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-16-ask-where-attention-is-design.md) lists 'the only signal is an inferred terminal turn (Codex, Grok)' as unsure. `suggest` reads 'only' literally: an inferred turn gives Clax, unsure (surface.rs:240-247) only when no Clax signal exists at all: no tab input or focused report, and no act of the person's own behind the last delivery (a comment they wrote, an answer, a skip or Ask me here, at its own time; a delivery's own time never counts); an inferred turn newer than the newest Clax signal by TIE_SECS or more gives Terminal, clear (surface.rs:248-275), exactly as a typed prompt would, and within TIE_SECS it is a tie (Clax, unsure). The other reading would make every inferred turn at most unsure (Terminal, unsure or Clax, unsure), on the grounds that a turn without a prompt hook may be an agent's own continuation rather than the person typing. Covered by surface::tests::an_inferred_turn_alone_is_unsure. Needs the owner to confirm which reading the spec means.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":240},"end":{"line":275},"content_hash":"a285fa2dd8930f4dfaa13bf4154088ba88027ca1fc3926222e13f5d008c0cdb7"},"summary":"Never let an inferred terminal turn give a clear terminal suggestion","supersedes":"cede921d518734492f67058bc2ad66623a335a7c0b8473d5c2bdddeb92e5176a","tags":["revisit:a Codex, Grok or Pi session is suggested the terminal (clear) while its person was in Clax","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.424224Z","id":"37c1c5bdadc96572a62a2b2752511416ebfe03d26060335818325e450d76faf0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:7e1ac2f2e","summary":"Fixed: Signals carries the person's act (clax_core::surface::Act, ActKind wrote|answered|skipped|pulled) apart from the Delivery, and the why names it ('answered this session's question in Clax', 'skipped', 'pressed Ask me here on'), naming a thread only for a written comment. Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test --test_arg=surface:: passes surface::tests::the_why_names_the_persons_act_as_it_was, and api_where_to_ask::a_late_answer_is_the_persons_act_in_clax_at_its_answer asserts 'The person answered this session's question in Clax 0 s ago'.","supersedes":"143e782bffed945793df8052b556fae170e668f5c91d7dfd1067d08f49a1640b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:51.717277Z","id":"3f55d00ab3c1a4b4877bc0d309ad458c29a6eb7d963707b2e7cd14407007987d","body":{"detail":"In suggest (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs:240-275) the Clax side is the newest of Signals.clax_at (tab input or focused report) and Signals.act (the person's own comment, answer, skip or Ask me here behind the last delivery, at its own time; a delivery's own time never counts), with no age limit. With no Clax signal at all, an inferred turn 5 s ago gives Clax, unsure (surface.rs:240-247); add a Clax input from an hour ago and the same turn gives Terminal, clear (surface.rs:248-275). An option for the owner: count only Clax signals within QUIET_SECS when deciding whether the inferred turn is the only signal, so a stale Clax signal leaves the turn unsure.","kind":"comment","references":"8ccc53cd496662b83fc1d8f745d0d65c0ea8869651b353898812f34666eee5ca","summary":"The reading has an asymmetry: a Clax signal of any age turns an inferred turn from unsure to Terminal, clear","supersedes":"d5fc0c930a5a1a1c599e143934854e3f95f8defc8942df49f63a94ca7ae69279","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.618463Z","id":"2871aa79224853075673f43b4cb909899a1433126831648291d9b05cf455199d","body":{"detail":"suggest (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs, the quiet closure and the match below it) gives Clax, unsure, whenever neither side has a signal newer than QUIET_SECS. A person who types a long prompt and then watches the terminal for more than 5 minutes, with no further prompt, is suggested Clax (unsure), though their attention never left the terminal. Signals closer than TIE_SECS are likewise unsure and lean to Clax. Both windows were chosen without data on how people move between the terminal and Clax.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":11},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"4bd7a40a1aa6b156d141d0a200b81cad00e358a8298b6bc9b4d1d7c652a19912"},"summary":"TIE_SECS (60) and QUIET_SECS (300) are a default to tune with use, not a measured value","tags":["tuning","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:55:11.275859Z","id":"4ef46d08062496dce479b254edb472278e981b7f22123e99d4ab1bb88f32e18f","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":133},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"0ef1131edb11791af6e810b02fda9491952e804ae8964af6b351b3f734f158d0"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"54ac59bced39bbd2b746a9d94180180cf0e9729d57af1a38fd06c7cbf3a3b2f9","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:19:01.873295Z","id":"a3215911038d25851f05fcb3cfcca60f4e1961f7d611a4d1a7d9f68b371c566b","body":{"detail":"capabilities::validate has no artifact ID, so it runs ReadDecl::check, which skips the self check that ReadDecl::from_capabilities makes. Publish (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs validate) and PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid> (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs patch) therefore store such a declaration; Store::may_read (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs) then parses it with the ID, fails, and answers NotDeclared for every source (a self-listing share shares with no one). Safe (fails closed) but silent for the page author.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"d0dc3709f12ea74023dc29f0f5310b9740d771b43db046dfa758cacce717e513"},"suggested_fix":"Run ReadDecl::from_capabilities(caps, id) where the ID is known: the PATCH handler and a publish to an existing artifact; a create has no ID yet, so nothing can name it.","summary":"A db.read or db.share.read list naming its own artifact is accepted at publish and PATCH, then grants nothing","tags":["validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:25:37.013507Z","id":"cbda9622e865936c18491ce357e1001d066d5d88d2bf5222d29aefdb31ab9c4e","body":{"detail":"Reproduced against a scratch daemon built from 652f225fcffa: PATCH /api/artifacts/<A> with {\"capabilities\":{\"db\":{\"read\":[\"<B>\",\"<A>\"]}}} answers 200 and stores the list. The spec (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-12-flutter-app-design.md §3.8, 'not itself') and the plan's ReadDecl interface both call this invalid_capabilities. The failure is wider than the self entry: Store::may_read (crates/clax-core/src/store/grants.rs:155) rejects the whole declaration, so one self entry silently turns every legitimate source in db.read into NotDeclared, and the page author (usually the agent) gets no error to correct. Fail-closed, so not a security hole, but a correctness defect the shell and agent tasks would surface as an unexplained not_declared.","kind":"comment","references":"a3215911038d25851f05fcb3cfcca60f4e1961f7d611a4d1a7d9f68b371c566b","suggested_fix":"Check in the store where the ID is known, so HTTP, MCP and CLI all get it: run ReadDecl::from_capabilities(caps, id) before the capabilities_json write in update_meta (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs, the UPDATE near line 254) and in the publish commit for an existing artifact (the UPDATE near line 1002), returning invalid_capabilities. Test both through the HTTP routes (PATCH and publish --id) with a self-listing db.read and db.share.read.","summary":"Review of 652f225fcffa: fix this in the R3 task, not later","tags":["review","validation","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:28:37.695362Z","id":"c1d83003d76d671acf8ede14e5c9306975d6519aa2c0384be0dc6e9ed69f06ba","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Store::update_meta and Store::write_version_from (crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs) now run ReadDecl::from_capabilities(caps, id) before writing, so PATCH and a publish to an existing artifact answer 400 invalid_capabilities for a db.read or db.share.read naming the artifact. Evidence: `cargo nextest run -p clax-server -E 'test(/a_read_declaration_naming/)'` passed (1 passed; it failed with status 200 before the change); full `cargo nextest run -p clax-core -p clax-server`: 1216 passed.","supersedes":"a3215911038d25851f05fcb3cfcca60f4e1961f7d611a4d1a7d9f68b371c566b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/icon.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364975Z","id":"1b9bdebb48057b716b23f066ed72b94b680dcd946bc4a385cab57ceed827f4f0","body":{"detail":"problem() walks with roxmltree's iterative descendants() and answers None for '<svg …>' + '<g>'*4500 + '</g>'*4500 + '</svg>'. Under `dart run`, iconProblem and cleanIcon both throw StackOverflowError on it (3,000 levels pass); the app's recursion (_namespaceProblem at apps/clax_app/lib/agent/icon_svg.dart:418, cleanIcon's clean, toXmlString) has the isolate's stack as its limit, which on a phone may be lower. write_file then fails with an Error rather than a ToolInputError, app_icon.dart's want() swallows it, and bundle_reader.dart:161 lets it escape the bundle read. Since any client may now publish such an icon and the core is the authority, the two disagree on input the shared vectors do not cover.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":173},"end":{"line":206},"content_hash":"8edf22394a3f25fdb7d816bbcdd28370f073e73559153b242327f7bc3e46a9d7"},"suggested_fix":"Add a depth rule to both (e.g. code nesting, at most 64 levels) checked before the walks, with a bad-too-deep-nesting fixture in crates/clax-core/tests/fixtures/icons.","summary":"Nesting depth is unbounded: the core accepts an icon of 4,500 nested <g> (31.5 KB) that the app's iconProblem and cleanIcon throw StackOverflowError on","tags":["review","icon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/icon.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:11.558902Z","id":"24beb5e7955fe78187e51e8563c363b71debcee1d8b61a70d9daca330d67583d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Both sides refuse past 64 levels with rule nesting, read from the text before any parse by the same scan (roxmltree itself recursed per level and overflowed a 2 MB thread on bad-nesting-stack-deep); cleanIcon refuses it too and the app's namespace walk is iterative. Vectors ok-nesting-at-limit, ok-nesting-markup, bad-nesting-too-deep, bad-nesting-unclosed, bad-nesting-stack-deep (4,600 levels). icon::tests and icon_fixtures_test.dart failed on them first and pass.","supersedes":"1b9bdebb48057b716b23f066ed72b94b680dcd946bc4a385cab57ceed827f4f0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.546111Z","id":"15ec208c27859a371337dc19147842ff91b4ced4079e0fe8e6b50ed4aa4b2c1d","body":{"detail":"The declaration a publish and a restore may set is checked by two copies of the same code (validated here, validate at line 298): a rule added to one (a title or icon word check, say) misses the other. RestoreDeclaration has title, icon, capabilities, label and note but no description, while PublishRequest and PATCH /api/artifacts/<aid> take one; RestoreBody (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:855) flattens it without deny_unknown_fields, so {\"description\": ...} or {\"files\": ...} on versions:restore is accepted and ignored with a 201. Nothing unchecked reaches the files (the declaration has no files), but a caller cannot tell a field it sent from one that was dropped.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":103},"end":{"line":138},"content_hash":"28cbf4dfc9784f94ff5c354d889fdcbf6f1ca70cf73db062fea56e13fffd5454"},"suggested_fix":"One Declaration struct (title, description, icon, capabilities, label, note) with one validate, flattened into PublishRequest and RestoreBody alike; refuse unknown fields on versions:restore (a hand-written check, since serde's deny_unknown_fields does not work with flatten).","summary":"RestoreDeclaration::validated copies validate()'s capability, label and note rules, and RestoreBody's flatten drops any other field silently, description among them","tags":["review","api","restore","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/icon.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.546694Z","id":"6cb07c0f222db8ecf9d83fb2064bd75aaa60f61ddcb2bbf370659ce589501455","body":{"detail":"The file is deterministic today: a fixed xorshift seed, the vectors sorted by name, and serde_json's default BTreeMap writing keys sorted (code, from, message, svg). serde_json::json! builds a serde_json::Map, whose order is a crate feature unified across the workspace (and across crate_universe under Bazel); with preserve_order it becomes insertion order (from, svg, code, message) and the byte comparison with the checked-in file fails. The Dart side (apps/clax_app/test/agent/icon_fixtures_test.dart) reads it by key and is unaffected.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":806},"end":{"line":817},"content_hash":"dfea7f47ff1e5eeed6782061d30b6d613923497bd29808b23766b4b6d0a78600"},"suggested_fix":"Serialize a struct with fixed field order (#[derive(Serialize)] struct Mutation { from, svg, code, message }) instead of json!.","summary":"mutations.json's bytes depend on serde_json's map order: a dependency that turns on serde_json's preserve_order feature reorders every object and fails the_mutations_file_holds_the_cores_answers with no rule changed","tags":["review","tests","icons","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:26:11.540804Z","id":"baec5b5d61af155adf8bc2be61b6752b02d19643a266af6861303e3a5b4549a6","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: validate() and RestoreDeclaration::validated both call check_declared (capabilities, label, note). RestoreBody collects any other field and the route answers 400 invalid_args naming it. crates/clax-server/tests/api_restore.rs restore_refuses_a_field_it_does_not_take_naming_it (description, files) failed with 201 and passes now (//crates/clax-server:integration__*); //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"15ec208c27859a371337dc19147842ff91b4ced4079e0fe8e6b50ed4aa4b2c1d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/icon.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:26:11.699179Z","id":"a4ab9eff88eb455d8aeac338771a54da55da18808885b0b10a978f04f0e2752d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:652f225fcffa","summary":"Fixed: mutations.json is written from a Mutation struct (code, from, message, svg, the checked-in order), so serde_json's map order no longer reaches it; the file is unchanged and icon::tests::the_mutations_file_holds_the_cores_answers passes (//crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test).","supersedes":"6cb07c0f222db8ecf9d83fb2064bd75aaa60f61ddcb2bbf370659ce589501455","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/gitctx_capture_tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T15:43:35.961850Z","id":"f16b749c98631226db5d4d33c2d1103e6b43eec98cd005acbf51e8baa560d3ec","body":{"detail":"In a bazelisk test of //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test beside //crates/clax-store, //crates/clax-http and //crates/clax-server/... (2026-10-19), it failed at crates/clax-core/src/gitctx_capture_tests.rs:864 with '4 runs'; rerun alone (--cache_test_results=no) it passed. capture() under soon() may stop before its fifth git command when the machine is loaded, so the count depends on timing; asserting on the commands that ran, or capturing with no deadline, would remove it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":844},"end":{"line":864},"content_hash":"0f2c56edafbd7ad6c787cf97b9b7982f4329c42e043dee63b6c8eb78504d5a1a"},"summary":"Load flake: every_command_runs_with_the_pins_and_a_cleared_environment saw 4 git runs where it asserts at least 5","tags":["flake","session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179596Z","id":"617da899235dc181ccc9d6b72a643d5e0b4acb13199eee5627530d9e0f7434bf","body":{"detail":"validate checks `label.chars().count() > MAX_LABEL_CHARS` (publish.rs:264-271) and nothing else on the text fields: `title`, `description` and `icon` go to ValidatedPublish unchanged (publish.rs:347-351). require_title (publish.rs:246-254) only refuses a blank title. The metadata route has the same gap: PatchBody in crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:577-584 hands title/description/icon to MetaPatch with only capabilities validated, and Store::update_meta (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs) adds no bound. A publish body may be tens of MiB (MAX_BODY_BYTES is 64 MiB of decoded files, publish.rs:11), so one agent or page can set a multi-megabyte title that every gallery listing, `/api/stream` Version delta (events.rs:18-21 carries `title`), agent payload and the `<title>` of shell pages then repeats; a title holding U+202E or newlines renders reversed or breaks one-line views. html_title, by contrast, caps derived titles at MAX_DERIVED_TITLE_CHARS (200, publish.rs:150) and collapses whitespace.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":260},"end":{"line":271},"content_hash":"60a00f46f94f87c12691cfdd5742c76323ed06f790e75cdf445161baa113a6fe"},"suggested_fix":"Add MAX_TITLE_CHARS (200, matching MAX_DERIVED_TITLE_CHARS), MAX_DESCRIPTION_CHARS and MAX_ICON_CHARS to publish.rs and one `check_text_fields` helper that refuses longer values and control or format characters (gitctx::text's rule, gitctx.rs:129-136); call it from validate and from the PATCH metadata route so both write paths share it.","summary":"publish::validate bounds the label (60 characters) but not title, description or icon, which it passes through with any length and any control or bidi character","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/working.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179704Z","id":"611a5dc27b4f13b469ac616fb95caaf6c2dcd00a3c420af84227f830f47bea89","body":{"detail":"clean_line filters `!c.is_control()`, which is Unicode category Cc only; U+202A-U+202E, U+2066-U+2069 (bidi embeddings, overrides, isolates), zero-width characters and tag characters (category Cf) pass through. It cleans text other people read: a viewer's presence `where` (presence.rs:234), a send batch's note (crates/clax-store/src/batches.rs:96), version and draft notes (publish.rs:282, crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs:243) and working messages. The crate already treats these characters as a spoofing risk elsewhere: names::has_bidi_control (names.rs:164-171) for display names, and gitctx::text with is_format_char (gitctx.rs:125-163) for git context, whose doc says they 'could make rendered output read differently from what was stored'. Example: a note stored as `fixed \\u{202E}etadpu` displays as `fixed update` in the changelog, while an agent reading the stored text sees `etadpu`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":286},"end":{"line":305},"content_hash":"5ac0db58f677f28d0e071f9d8525a8cbea5310ca7664a5daf28e9bb72eab5278"},"suggested_fix":"Make clean_line also drop the characters gitctx::is_format_char matches (move that predicate to a shared text module), keeping LRM/RLM/ALM if right-to-left text needs them as names.rs does, and add a test with U+202E and U+200B input.","summary":"clean_line drops control characters but keeps bidi overrides and other format characters, so viewer-written one-line text can render as different text","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179742Z","id":"a3465b4759601706886606b94f664a84e5d7ccaee8bd1db450fa11bc9eedcf59","body":{"detail":"`crate::Store` and `crate::Delivery` are clax-store items (the store moved out of clax-core; lib.rs:5 says the SQLite store is clax-store's). The intra-doc links that still name them do not resolve: error.rs:67 (`crate::Store::open_on`), content/mod.rs:4, :78, :423, :607 (`crate::Store`, `reconcile_pushes_async`, `call_async`), events.rs:69 and feedback.rs:77, :255 (`crate::Delivery::view`/`people`; clax-core's only Delivery is surface::Delivery, surface.rs:67, which has neither method). `grep -rn 'crate::Delivery\\|crate::Store' crates/clax-core/src` lists all eight. The variants ReadTimeout, TaskFailed, NestedJob, WouldBlock and SchemaNewer (error.rs:60-91) describe only clax-store's executor and migrations, so a change to that executor has to edit clax-core's shared error type.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"31012f31442e28ab01f0a70a0e77f43e6ca475b7fad149be0849a9f234d115d4"},"suggested_fix":"Rewrite the eight links as `clax_store::Store::…` in plain backticks (clax-core cannot link to a crate above it), and add `cargo doc`/`bazel` rustdoc with `-D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links` to a lane so the next move is caught.","summary":"Eight doc links in clax-core point at crate::Store and crate::Delivery, which this crate does not define, and the CoreError variants they document are clax-store's","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179774Z","id":"ff4a0a8b1624e4aad58074f22f34e816b28780023702b3f8a30ce51d16f6cb3b","body":{"detail":"lib.rs:1-5: 'The SQLite store is `clax-store`'s; nothing here runs a query.' perf.rs:10-89 opens an in-memory rusqlite Connection, creates tables, inserts 15,000 rows and runs QUERY, for the daemon latency gate (`POST /api/admin/perf/calibrate`). Its own doc (perf.rs:1-7) says it must use 'the same bundled SQLite and build flags as the store', which is a property of clax-store's rusqlite dependency, not of clax-core. Keeping it here is one of the two reasons clax-core links rusqlite at all (the other is CoreError::Db, error.rs:95).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":5},"content_hash":"1744d115cdf19593d486930ac47a9495b91d3f2e02c8fa77b841b607c2c0a80e"},"suggested_fix":"Move perf.rs to clax-store (next to the connection setup whose flags it must match) and re-export it there, or, if it stays, change lib.rs's sentence to name the calibration read as the one exception.","summary":"The crate doc says nothing in clax-core runs a query, but perf::Calibration builds and queries a SQLite database here","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179847Z","id":"fbaaf72ec7e120a3d67235177b6b0f6c5187e2d980aadf49a4e168213d6b5edf","body":{"detail":"rights.rs:15-17: 'counted before merging, with a preset name counting as all of its objects (`clax:collaborator` alone is nine)'. Rights::preset returns `Rights(merge(rights))` (rights.rs:501), and parse_with extends `out` with that merged vector (rights.rs:457) before the MAX_ACCESS check (rights.rs:460). Merging joins Artifacts {read}+{create} at `*` and Comments {read,reply,watch}+{write,resolve,send} at `*`, leaving 7 objects: Artifacts{read,create}@*, Artifacts{update,delete}@own, Comments(6)@*, Db{read}@* view, Db{read,write}@* interact, Db{read,write}@own admin, Ask. So a client can send the preset plus nine objects, not seven, and the documented budget is wrong.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"dbd7f6a7346e759f21c596fa04d3ad0c8b67a8a6d293d15d3377ade5b2d021ae"},"suggested_fix":"Either count presets unmerged (build the preset's Vec without merge for counting) or change the doc to 'a preset counts as its merged objects (clax:reader is four, clax:collaborator seven)', and pin the count with a test.","summary":"The rights limit doc says clax:collaborator alone counts as nine access objects, but Rights::preset merges it to seven before parse_with counts it","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179880Z","id":"939313d345951e80b58052c4b6095f456b10af579cb9668186c33cafbd4aa857","body":{"detail":"new_credential (extension.rs:100-107) is secret::token(CREDENTIAL_PREFIX) re-implemented with rand::rng() instead of the OS source, and credential_hash (extension.rs:110-116) is secret::sha256_hex re-implemented. secret.rs:5-9 promises that a minted secret 'has no Display or Serialize, so a log line, an error or an event cannot carry one by accident' and that 'every code is drawn from the operating system's random source'; extension credentials get neither guarantee because they are Strings (callers: crates/clax-store/src/extension.rs:45, crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs:636). rand::rng() is a CSPRNG, so this is not a weakness today, but a later `tracing::debug!(?cred)` would print it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":116},"content_hash":"140c0d71fe95f664d34528b696e88c60f1809207e5b5c7c112673862dc892495"},"suggested_fix":"Return `Secret` from new_credential via `crate::secret::token(CREDENTIAL_PREFIX)`, define credential_hash as `crate::secret::sha256_hex`, and expose the value only where it is handed to the extension.","summary":"Extension credentials are minted and hashed by a second copy of secret.rs's helpers that returns a plain String instead of a Secret","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:00:30.179978Z","id":"939cbc074262c3d0f8934bc0c969ccedc86793cf2af9c7e50a89cc6cfeaccab2","body":{"detail":"db.rs:2-3 reads 'db.d.ts 0.2.61 (shipped under web/contract/ from Task 5)'. No document in the repository defines Task 5, so the parenthesis tells the reader nothing; the contract it means is web/contract/0.2.61/ (present in the tree). gitctx_capture_tests.rs:339 has the same kind of reference ('plan Task 12, step 3').","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"7e06d379af13f5944a57fc1935d533ba90a80f90d6b4ac0a061a612517b5815d"},"suggested_fix":"Replace the parenthesis with the path, e.g. 'web/contract/0.2.61/db.d.ts, \"PATH GRAMMAR\" and \"ACCESS RULES\"', and drop the plan reference in gitctx_capture_tests.rs:339.","summary":"The db module doc cites 'Task 5', a step of an implementation plan the repository does not hold","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.199884Z","id":"b8ce5fc4a7b66f141665dd61b805bdf0cfbbce7f0e94cd32234751cc081ebf53","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:264-271 is the only length check (label vs MAX_LABEL_CHARS); :346-349 copies req.title, req.description, req.icon into ValidatedPublish unchanged; require_title (:246-254) only refuses blank. crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs PatchBody (title/description/icon: Option<String>) is handed on at :647-649 with no check, and Store::update_meta (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs:257) adds none. `grep -rn 'MAX_TITLE\\|MAX_DESCRIPTION\\|MAX_ICON' --include='*.rs' crates` finds only routes/live.rs MAX_TITLE (live sessions) and questions.rs MAX_DESCRIPTION, neither on the artifact path. Kind concern fits.","kind":"comment","references":"617da899235dc181ccc9d6b72a643d5e0b4acb13199eee5627530d9e0f7434bf","summary":"confirmed: validate bounds only the label; title, description and icon pass through unbounded and unfiltered","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/working.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.200063Z","id":"b9b1271863ab2894fb126a324cf2bd6ce3c257f788f3cc1f1b24ae81c0b80744","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/working.rs:290-294 keeps `c.is_whitespace() || !c.is_control()`; Rust's char::is_control is general category Cc, so U+202E/U+200B (Cf) are kept. Callers on viewer- or agent-written text: presence.rs:234, publish.rs:282, crates/clax-server/src/routes/drafts.rs:243, crates/clax-store/src/batches.rs:96, crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs:399, crates/clax-server/src/routes/working.rs:103. The crate rejects these elsewhere: names.rs:168-171 has_bidi_control, gitctx.rs:128-163 text/is_format_char.","kind":"comment","references":"611a5dc27b4f13b469ac616fb95caaf6c2dcd00a3c420af84227f830f47bea89","summary":"confirmed: clean_line filters only char::is_control (Cc), so bidi overrides and zero-width characters survive","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.200215Z","id":"3762b7961c4c215464cc003586de7628a74752c21e955e1db380d96b2c8f943d","body":{"detail":"`grep -rn 'crate::Delivery\\|crate::Store' crates/clax-core/src` (excluding .qual) lists error.rs:67, content/mod.rs:4,:78,:423,:607, events.rs:69, feedback.rs:77,:255. crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs:75-88 re-exports no Store or Delivery; the only Delivery is surface::Delivery (surface.rs:67), and `grep -n 'fn view\\|fn people' crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs` finds nothing. error.rs:60-91 variants ReadTimeout..SchemaNewer document clax-store's executor (`clax_store::exec::READ_LIMIT`).","kind":"comment","references":"a3465b4759601706886606b94f664a84e5d7ccaee8bd1db450fa11bc9eedcf59","summary":"confirmed: eight intra-doc links name crate::Store / crate::Delivery, which clax-core does not define with those methods","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.200364Z","id":"bd5d71fa9ca6b766f9914873532a11adca36d9e1ebec5b92a27c170f4826b932","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs:4-5: 'The SQLite store is `clax-store`'s; nothing here runs a query.' crates/clax-core/src/perf.rs:1-30 imports rusqlite::Connection and defines QUERY (a SELECT over tables t and c). `grep -rln rusqlite crates/clax-core/src` lists only perf.rs and error.rs; crates/clax-core/Cargo.toml:24 depends on rusqlite.","kind":"comment","references":"ff4a0a8b1624e4aad58074f22f34e816b28780023702b3f8a30ce51d16f6cb3b","summary":"confirmed: lib.rs says nothing here runs a query, yet perf.rs builds and queries an in-memory SQLite database","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.200516Z","id":"72067f6894ddb715e2d22fb6ebdb8820b64d6b2d583e4236fab46021729d8fb5","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs:15-17 says nine. preset() (:477-501) builds 9 Access objects and returns Rights(merge(rights)); parse_with (:457) extends `out` with that merged vector before the MAX_ACCESS check (:460). merge (:687-707) keys on (kind, level, locations) then (kind, level, actions): Artifacts {read}+{create} at Any join, Comments {read,reply,watch}+{write,resolve,send} at Any join; Artifacts update/delete@Own, three Db objects (levels View, Interact, Admin differ) and Ask stay separate: 7.","kind":"comment","references":"fbaaf72ec7e120a3d67235177b6b0f6c5187e2d980aadf49a4e168213d6b5edf","summary":"confirmed: clax:collaborator counts as seven objects, not nine, because preset() merges before parse_with counts","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.200669Z","id":"d78b38fc19fbeeeabcb2a3b24709e82aa222e61425d4290a951acc866e5905b7","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/extension.rs:100-107 fills 32 bytes from rand::rng() and formats prefix + URL_SAFE_NO_PAD base64, returning String; :110-116 hex-encodes Sha256. crates/clax-core/src/secret.rs:93-95 token(prefix) does the same from getrandom (random_bytes, :82-86) and returns Secret, whose doc (:5-9) promises no Display/Serialize. Callers take the String: crates/clax-store/src/extension.rs:45-46, crates/clax-http/src/extension.rs:636. Kind suggestion fits.","kind":"comment","references":"939313d345951e80b58052c4b6095f456b10af579cb9668186c33cafbd4aa857","summary":"confirmed: new_credential and credential_hash duplicate secret::token and secret::sha256_hex but return a plain String","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/db.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T16:02:12.200972Z","id":"a1c68a04a2569be1d21ba5786a11c650702e428434594f17069947a418580c89","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/db.rs:2-3: 'db.d.ts 0.2.61 (shipped under web/contract/ from Task 5)'; crates/clax-core/src/gitctx_capture_tests.rs:339: '(plan Task 12, step 3)'. web/contract/0.2.61/ exists.","kind":"comment","references":"939cbc074262c3d0f8934bc0c969ccedc86793cf2af9c7e50a89cc6cfeaccab2","summary":"confirmed: db.rs module doc cites 'Task 5', and gitctx_capture_tests.rs cites 'plan Task 12, step 3'","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/brief.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:07:07.075112Z","id":"6f77e9df922434c5d33d23a283688eef95b11e5ca704eabed2f8ec418f068967","body":{"detail":"check_title runs crate::gitctx::text, which refuses every character in crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs is_format_char, including U+200C (ZERO WIDTH NON-JOINER, required in Persian words such as 'mi‌xaham') and U+200D (ZERO WIDTH JOINER, inside emoji such as a family or profession emoji); formProblem (web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts:36) refuses all of \\p{Cf} likewise. Such a title is 400 invalid_title / 'A title is one line of plain text.', though a page's own <title> with them is accepted as an artifact title by publish (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs html_title). The aim stated in the doc comment (line breaks, bidi controls) needs only Cc and the bidi controls U+202A-202E, U+2066-2069, U+200E-200F, U+061C.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"d4a4484f591397733b061f4e8c9df97c829b7881c9c5a8e8c29b7f9f8bef57f6"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse controls and the bidi and invisible-spoofing characters, and allow U+200C and U+200D (in both check_title and formProblem).","summary":"Titles refuse ZWNJ and ZWJ, which Persian and Indic words and emoji sequences need","tags":["review","review:new-artifact","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/brief.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:10:48.580512Z","id":"e0ee54d79a36e108225509b1b8d7eeb6a71a572424fb3d5a5cdd665a84d5ea33","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/brief.rs:29 calls crate::gitctx::text, which refuses any is_format_char (crates/clax-core/src/gitctx.rs:133); that list includes '\\u{200B}'..='\\u{200F}' (gitctx.rs:151), covering ZWNJ U+200C and ZWJ U+200D. web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts:36 refuses /[\\p{Cc}\\p{Cf}]/u, and both are Cf. crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs:160-201 html_title only collapses whitespace and decodes entities, so a page <title> with them is kept as the artifact title.","kind":"comment","references":"6f77e9df922434c5d33d23a283688eef95b11e5ca704eabed2f8ec418f068967","summary":"confirmed: check_title and formProblem refuse U+200C and U+200D","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/brief.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.247020Z","id":"6cd9c8c5deaf62966471fb668428172652fe913eac42537e365999d69494bac2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fde24fc8c","summary":"Fixed: check_title refuses controls and format characters but U+200C and U+200D; formProblem (web/shell/src/view/new-artifact.ts) does the same. Evidence: //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test passes brief::tests (a Persian word with ZWNJ and a ZWJ family emoji accepted, U+200B and U+2066 refused), api_briefs::an_artifact_started_from_a_brief_names_who_started_it_to_people creates a ZWNJ title, and //web:unit passes the 'titles' cases.","supersedes":"6f77e9df922434c5d33d23a283688eef95b11e5ca704eabed2f8ec418f068967","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:09:25.882852Z","id":"cb1b58faa8f4807cebd561aaa850f4c19a26a7e78f8eee224bff13073b134c3e","body":{"detail":"clax_core::content stays in clax-core: it is a trait and two implementations with no SQLite, implemented again by clax-content-git and crates/clax-worker, which would otherwise depend on clax-store and link rusqlite for it. The layout spec (section 2.1) names clax-store 'the SQLite store'; content is the files beside it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"a19f42794e98e4b4ae69b98d2c2d12f03da6b0c5668d5006647ab7a845a08990"},"summary":"Move the ContentStore trait and its fs and memory stores into clax-store","supersedes":"fad4f4b6e699693cae00be7f5822cefe848579b371bdfe4baaeaa0534ee7fb19","tags":["layout","revisit:a content store implementation needs the store's tables","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:01.317043Z","id":"6cbcb59498f83b2c8ed3364a03ebc8dd0773cd5d3e446bda67f562dd2e57245e","body":{"detail":"error.rs:67, content/mod.rs:4, :78, :423, :607, events.rs:69 and feedback.rs:77, :255 now read `clax_store::Store::…` / `clax_store::Delivery::…` without link brackets (clax-core cannot link to a crate above it). `grep -rn 'crate::Delivery\\|crate::Store' crates/clax-core/src` (excluding .qual) lists nothing. Not done: a rustdoc lane with -D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links, and moving the store-only CoreError variants out of clax-core; both are recorded as a concern on error.rs:60:91.","kind":"comment","references":"a3465b4759601706886606b94f664a84e5d7ccaee8bd1db450fa11bc9eedcf59","summary":"partly fixed: the eight crate::Store / crate::Delivery links now name clax_store items in plain backticks","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:01.319991Z","id":"af47d35f90bd678c2141177201838d6491ee956c6c950c395289140ca600a7a8","body":{"detail":"ReadTimeout, TaskFailed, NestedJob, WouldBlock and SchemaNewer (error.rs:60-91) describe only clax-store's executor (`clax_store::exec`) and migrations, so a change there edits clax-core's shared error type. Separately, no `just` recipe or Bazel target runs rustdoc with `-D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links` (grep -rn 'rustdoc' justfile scripts finds none), so links to items that move out of a crate (eight did, before being rewritten in plain backticks) are not caught. Moving the variants means a store error type that converts into CoreError at the HTTP boundary; adding the lane means a rustdoc build per crate in CI time.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":91},"content_hash":"6349a18a1c9e410c95cfb43bfc8a7c95e2f81bb5dd44837160f8730fd31f9e91"},"summary":"CoreError holds clax-store's executor and migration failures, and no lane catches broken intra-doc links","tags":["revisit:the next change to clax-store's executor errors, or when a rustdoc lane is added","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:45:01.323236Z","id":"bcb0f194ce6027a068eefde60fe3bd852f69833e4e1e574855a61383409e3314","body":{"detail":"check_meta_text (crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs) runs from validate and from the PATCH metadata route (crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs patch). Codes: title_too_long, description_too_long, icon_too_long; invalid_args for a control character (line breaks and tabs included) or a character text::is_hidden_char matches (bidi embeddings, overrides and isolates, zero-width spaces, tags). ZWJ/ZWNJ and LRM/RLM/ALM pass, so emoji sequences and right-to-left titles publish. html_title (and plugins/pi/src/clax.ts htmlTitle, fixture plugins/pi/test/fixtures/contract.json) drops the same characters, so a page without an explicit title still publishes. A blank title is left to require_title, so creating with \"  \\n\" still answers 'title is required'. Nothing in the daemon, MCP tools (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs PublishArgs), Pi plugin (plugins/pi/src/clax.ts) or web shell bounded these fields before; the web shell's patchArtifact sends only `pinned`. docs/contract.md lists the bounds and codes. The numbers are a judgment call: 200 matches MAX_DERIVED_TITLE_CHARS and routes/live.rs MAX_TITLE; 1000 and 40 fit a one-line description and one icon word. Tests: publish::tests::bounds_title_description_and_icon, api_artifacts::patch_and_delete.","kind":"comment","references":"617da899235dc181ccc9d6b72a643d5e0b4acb13199eee5627530d9e0f7434bf","summary":"fixed: publish::check_meta_text bounds title (200), description (1000) and icon (40) and refuses control and hidden format characters, on publish and PATCH","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:14:21.285558Z","id":"ea213decce3c6aa8dc61d2aaf98ba9d832ec36517904b313a53398cb1afb8e18","body":{"detail":"Today publish::check_meta_text refuses with invalid_args a title, description or icon holding any control character, line breaks included, on publish and on PATCH /api/artifacts/<id>. Before this check, a multi-line description was stored as sent.\n\nOption A (current): refuse. An agent learns at once that the description is one line (crates/clax-mcp/src/tools.rs PublishArgs documents it as 'One-line description'), and nothing is stored that one-line views would mangle. Cost: a publish that worked before now fails until the agent removes the line break.\n\nOption B: collapse whitespace the way a version note is cleaned (working::clean_line, as publish.rs does for `note`), or the way publish::fit_meta_text cleans pushed metadata. Line breaks and tabs become one space and hidden characters are dropped, while the length bound still refuses. Cost: the stored text differs from what was sent, silently.\n\nRecommendation: B for description (and for title on update), keeping A for icon. A description is prose that agents often wrap, the note field already behaves this way, and fit_meta_text already exists. The current behaviour stays at A until the owner decides.","kind":"comment","references":"bcb0f194ce6027a068eefde60fe3bd852f69833e4e1e574855a61383409e3314","summary":"Decision needed: refuse a description holding a line break, or collapse it to one line?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.339542Z","id":"dc4fc64bbfefdabe205bc32036bc3d242d9579bcf568cfe8affa991b1d415495","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:34ca3b8cb","summary":"Fixed (34ca3b8cb, d8cd59706, a4eed95c1, 2ce253f72): validate bounds title/description/icon (200/1000/40) and refuses control and hidden format characters; live titles and pushed metadata are fitted to the same checks; //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test and //crates/clax-server/... pass (api_live_sites::page_titles_with_hidden_characters_or_long_urls_are_kept_and_cut, public::tests::outgoing_metadata_is_fit_to_the_public_daemons_checks).","supersedes":"617da899235dc181ccc9d6b72a643d5e0b4acb13199eee5627530d9e0f7434bf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
