{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/extension.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.492806Z","id":"00982e872edcb3897ac8269fb68592bc3dcc86d6f9630befb402323d575e7a49","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2048d917a","summary":"Fixed: extension credentials are minted as Secrets from secret::token and hashed by secret.rs's helpers; //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test and //crates/clax-server/... pass.","supersedes":"939313d345951e80b58052c4b6095f456b10af579cb9668186c33cafbd4aa857","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T19:59:20.666016Z","id":"b4f6f47a6f8017a8eb1acece0d1f5913b95fc01f341e5436ddeb5d984b7c4055","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a3465b4759601706886606b94f664a84e5d7ccaee8bd1db450fa11bc9eedcf59","summary":"Partly fixed on main in 14cf0d25d: the doc links no longer name crate::Store or crate::Delivery. Moving clax-store's executor and migration variants out of CoreError is left to concern af47d35f.","tags":["session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:22:59.011865Z","id":"e2c31a84fe59d51c8f7b480d2a5594cda6b1a09bf205dbbf6004a3d033de06aa","body":{"detail":"clax_core::content stays in clax-core: it is a trait and two implementations with no SQLite, implemented again by clax-content-git and crates/clax-worker, which would otherwise depend on clax-store and link rusqlite for it. The layout spec (section 2.1) names clax-store 'the SQLite store'; content is the files beside it.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"a19f42794e98e4b4ae69b98d2c2d12f03da6b0c5668d5006647ab7a845a08990"},"summary":"Move the ContentStore trait and its fs and memory stores into clax-store","supersedes":"cb1b58faa8f4807cebd561aaa850f4c19a26a7e78f8eee224bff13073b134c3e","tags":["layout","revisit:a content store implementation needs the store's tables","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:53:17.992436Z","id":"944794426b61154c14e1404917b1b19248684df87a85de7f6ce5ed049eaef653","body":{"detail":"Failure: the owner makes a tag named 'T_ABCDEFGHJK' (or 't_ABCDEFGHJK'); then GET /api/artifacts?tag=t_abcdefghjk, naming another tag's real ID, also returns the artifacts carrying the 'T_ABCDEFGHJK' tag. is_id (crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs:87-91) checks the raw name against the lowercase alphabet only, so an upper-case variant passes; fold (to_lowercase) then turns it into the ID shape, and crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:399-406 carries_all matches a ref by ID or by folded name, so it matches both tags. resolve_in (crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:94-118) looks up IDs first, so writes stay unambiguous; only the filters, and docs/contract.md:1158-1160's promise that a tag is named 'by its ID or its name unambiguously', are wrong. Only the owner makes tags, so the impact is a confusing filter, not an escalation.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":127},"content_hash":"1b9ece28049d8547357fc27ce5ad528772fd072e6367af080444da120c44eb22"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse a name when is_id(&fold(name)) holds, and test it with 'T_' + ten upper-case alphabet characters.","summary":"A tag name that folds to a tag ID's shape passes check_name, so a filter by ID also matches the tag so named","tags":["review","review:artifact-tags","security","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:55:11.178185Z","id":"663015b4b27a54951a6b211451830196a284c0b622aead0b95a59c0beb44f667","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs:87-91 is_id strips the literal prefix 't_' and checks crate::ids::ALPHABET (crates/clax-core/src/ids.rs:9, b\"0123456789abcdefghjkmnpqrstvwxyz\", lowercase only); check_name (tags.rs:121) calls is_id(name) on the unfolded name, so 'T_ABCDEFGHJK' is accepted. fold (tags.rs:32) is to_lowercase. crates/clax-server/src/routes/artifacts.rs:412-417 filters GET /api/artifacts with carries_all on the raw refs, and crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:399-405 matches 't.id == r || fold(&t.name) == fold(r)', so ?tag=t_abcdefghjk matches both the tag with that ID and the tag named 'T_ABCDEFGHJK'. The inbox summary (crates/clax-server/src/routes/inbox.rs:495-508) passes IDs from tag_filter_ids into carries_all and has the same collision. resolve_in (crates/clax-store/src/tags.rs:94-101) tries IDs first, so writes resolve to one tag. Severity concern is right: only the owner names tags.","kind":"comment","references":"944794426b61154c14e1404917b1b19248684df87a85de7f6ce5ed049eaef653","summary":"confirmed: an upper-case 'T_ABCDEFGHJK' passes check_name and its folded name equals a tag ID shape, so ID filters match it","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/tags.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:14:34.274644Z","id":"201a5536f660c026aabb37ea078a4b09b2156b4491ca85e28828741c56f6becd","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cf149d9a4","summary":"Fixed in cf149d9a4: check_name refuses a name when is_id(&fold(name)) holds; tags::tests::names_are_trimmed_bounded_and_plain refuses 'T_ABCDEFGHJK' and 't_ABCDEFGHJK' (bazelisk test //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test PASSED)","supersedes":"944794426b61154c14e1404917b1b19248684df87a85de7f6ce5ed049eaef653","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:06:32.031893Z","id":"81d31d7922b6409ad078cf215c4e80d6167e492f5361fb2eb0924d6f2948d8f0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4ef46d08062496dce479b254edb472278e981b7f22123e99d4ab1bb88f32e18f","summary":"[hosted] now takes site_domain (HostedConfig::site_domain, crates/clax-core/src/config.rs), which hosted mode carries as Hosted::sites and the daemon looks site hosts up under (AppState::sites, crates/clax-http/src/host.rs SiteHosts). It is the replacement for a content origin in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md; content_origin itself is still Worker-only until that design retires it.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:18:19.109252Z","id":"449bff0b1e323b851eb0daae148f090fc930a85006a0114543a8e0bb39c59c5e","body":{"detail":"HomeConfig::hosted refuses a site_domain equal to the public origin's host, above it or under it (nested_names), but not a sibling: public clax.example.com with site_domain sites.example.com passes. Both then share the registrable domain example.com, so a site could set Domain=example.com cookies the public origin receives, against docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-clax-run-site-origins-design.md ('a registrable domain that shares nothing with clax.dev'). Telling registrable domains apart needs the Public Suffix List, which the config does not consult.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":575},"end":{"line":585},"content_hash":"27bbed11af3267a4ffc2014fdd72370b56c11de389d0b161a49c2ca8b85cbbda"},"summary":"A site_domain that is a sibling of the public host under a shared parent is accepted","tags":["revisit:the config gains a Public Suffix List lookup","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:15:08.354474Z","id":"96db9c80d2e037b63afdcd86b2f94f98d0b627c17f6af658deadc6a45d179392","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"449bff0b1e323b851eb0daae148f090fc930a85006a0114543a8e0bb39c59c5e","summary":"The rule now lives in clax_core::config::hosted_site_domain, which HomeConfig::hosted and the Worker's SITE_DOMAIN (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs sites_of) both call, so a sibling under a shared parent is accepted on the Worker too; deploy.mjs refuses one before a deploy (its shared-parent check).","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:15:08.354648Z","id":"a7682a31272faedc545c27bfdf872d3aa06e29b979b8d1ca84b222c1f1957c11","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"4ef46d08062496dce479b254edb472278e981b7f22123e99d4ab1bb88f32e18f","summary":"Proposed close (obsolete): the Worker no longer reads CONTENT_ORIGIN (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs builds hosted mode with Hosted::with_sites from SITE_DOMAIN, the same rule as [hosted] site_domain), so neither deployment gives content an origin of its own.","tags":["session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:26:56.719162Z","id":"c8dd99fbf998fa239253a42b9c093eee16e4d36aa4ad61d7da50b095f2d828c0","body":{"detail":"ClaxApp needs apple_team_id (the team that signs dev.empathic.clax for iOS and macOS), the SHA-256 fingerprint of the certificate that signs the Android release of dev.empathic.clax (Play App Signing's, if Google signs it), and the App Store and Play Store page URLs once the app is listed. Until they are set (Worker vars APPLE_TEAM_ID, ANDROID_PACKAGE, ANDROID_SHA256, IOS_STORE_URL, ANDROID_STORE_URL), /a/<id>/get offers only Open in Clax for Mac and Download .clax, and its link opens no app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":170},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"a4a8f124909c559b31c93c8c40e0fbeb64c084ca149204ba50d2d97649676c74"},"summary":"clax.dev's Apple team ID, Android signing fingerprint and store URLs are not chosen yet","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:00:04.845660Z","id":"5af86ece9d19043d4d5f3bcbdd045c67d3082b7b11997f5d20302e83d1e1092d","body":{"detail":"authors_of_anchor names only the authors of the anchored file. The hosted client supplies the anchor text, and Store::mirror_thread (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:606-609) checks only its shape. The local file's author is the person, so the owner's agents read it. Bob, a stranger on the hosted Clax, can open a thread on Mia's app with up to 2000 characters of quote plus prefix, suffix, name and area text. Her local agents read that text through comments_read, GET .../threads and feedback items (anchor), while his comment body is withheld. Before afcdea2f2 the device read threads through the hosted agent channel. There the first comment of such a thread was withheld, so Sync::mirror (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs first_seen) never brought the thread down. The same rule already lets a local unapproved person's anchor text reach the owner's agents (docs/contract.md:5331, 'a thread's anchor and clip the authors of the anchored file'). So whether a mirrored thread's anchor should also count its first commenter is a spec call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":184},"content_hash":"f65fd367a7103988c679e1b05a463e95498eb0f2b8ecb9e1ff726411c91c91d1"},"suggested_fix":"In authors_of_anchor, add the thread's first comment's remote_author when it has one, as authors_of_clip already does with the first commenter. A mirrored stranger's anchor is then withheld until the person approves that author.","summary":"A mirrored thread's anchor text (quote, prefix, suffix, name, area fingerprint) written by an unapproved hosted author reaches the local agents, because the anchor counts as the anchored file's authors","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:07:07.134912Z","id":"9e92aa8e2c2a855bd2eba461ef5b2922ff0f5719a8e63331eb47cdae54915559","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:a4b4e0cb2","references":"5af86ece9d19043d4d5f3bcbdd045c67d3082b7b11997f5d20302e83d1e1092d","summary":"Commit a4b4e0cb2 implements e7f3033f for anchors: authors_of_anchor (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs) adds the first comment's remote_author key, so a mirrored thread's anchor from an unapproved hosted author is withheld from the local agents like its body; local threads and the signed-in person's own mirrored threads are unchanged. Test: crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs a_strangers_mirrored_anchor_is_withheld_from_her_agents_until_approved (bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__5 passes; it checks the thread list, since, the single thread and feedback, then the release after approving remote:<origin>#<ID>). With the authors_of_anchor change reverted it fails at api_linked.rs:2530 (anchor_withheld null, quote 'Bob quoted this' visible). Left open for the owner to close.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:19:58.313884Z","id":"6fb4516bf3803b81087acf3e060272a6ff614cb16d3d2b2be89540617d35e73f","body":{"detail":"placeholder::anchor nulls quote, prefix, suffix, selector, custom_name, file and html_hash and drops area tag/text/children, but leaves Anchor.label (crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs:148-153, 'the quote as a person reads it') and Anchor.name (:154-160, the element's name) as written. The anchor is client-supplied, so a hosted author can put any text in label. The app's anchorSummary (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:2798-2818) uses anchor['label'] before anchor['quote'], and anchorLine goes into every FeedbackItem and CommentContext prompt line (lib/agent/loop.dart:1418, 2000; lib/queue/worker_agent.dart _commentsOf). So on a thread whose anchor is withheld (e.g. the person replies in a thread a stranger opened on clax.dev), the stranger's label reaches Claude: the opposite of the withhold-until-approved rule record 5af86ece describes ('quote, prefix, suffix, name, area fingerprint'). The app also does not read the thread's anchor_withheld flag, so it cannot drop the anchor itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":346},"end":{"line":372},"content_hash":"63165015303bdda590928f76292639cd3892574bbdbc057b840aebf182b82de8"},"suggested_fix":"Null label and name in placeholder::anchor (and assert both in crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs a_strangers_mirrored_anchor_is_withheld_from_her_agents_until_approved); in the app, parse anchor_withheld on ThreadView/FeedbackItem and render such an anchor as the whole artifact, so a field the core adds later fails closed.","summary":"A withheld anchor keeps its label and name, and the app's anchor line prints the label first, so a stranger's anchor text still reaches the agent's prompt","tags":["review","review:app-push-pull-deep","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T05:22:54.246091Z","id":"71d968b703ef791a3bfba104b42a8537e785f4f65cb6a8af9d03e9ff4e4abcf1","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:352-372 nulls quote, prefix, suffix, selector, custom_name, file, html_hash and strips area tag/text/children, nothing else; Anchor.label and Anchor.name (crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs:148-160) pass through. validate_label (anchor.rs:305-323) requires label to be the quote with only whitespace changed, so label carries exactly the withheld quote text; name is free text. apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart:2798-2818 anchorSummary uses anchor['label'] ?? anchor['quote']. grep -rn 'anchor_withheld\\|anchorWithheld' apps/clax_app/lib (Dart files) finds nothing, so the app cannot drop the anchor itself. Concern kind is right.","kind":"comment","references":"6fb4516bf3803b81087acf3e060272a6ff614cb16d3d2b2be89540617d35e73f","summary":"confirmed: placeholder::anchor leaves label and name, and the app's anchorSummary prints label before quote","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:22:29.026636Z","id":"1528ade350b5969cc6f9b0f4421db905f2d31798cbc679a68d438aa7f54cb832","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"6fb4516bf3803b81087acf3e060272a6ff614cb16d3d2b2be89540617d35e73f","summary":"The app half is fixed in a81bfa277: ThreadView.fromJson reads anchor_withheld, and FeedbackItem.fromJson a withheld anchor, as ThreadView.withheldAnchor ({kind: withheld}), which anchorSummary prints as 'a part of the page (withheld until the person approves its author)', so no label, name or later field of a withheld anchor reaches a prompt. Test: apps/clax_app/test/agent/loop_single_call_test.dart 'an anchor withheld from the agent shows none of its fields, from a thread read or a feedback item' (//apps/clax_app:agent_loop_single_call_test passes; with the anchor_withheld read removed it fails). The core half is open: at 567564ef8 placeholder::anchor (crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs:352-372) still leaves label and name.","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:29:28.739165Z","id":"6d42f4051a4968957025a1fd3f6198c18cf94d7c1ecd54c7403436fa9c11b572","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5b84bd376e8ccd4af41d9fad71ebbe77fc732d1f","summary":"placeholder::anchor now nulls label and name. Tests: crates/clax-store/src/visibility.rs placeholders_replace_fields_and_keep_the_object (label and name in, null out) and crates/clax-server/tests/api_linked.rs a_strangers_mirrored_anchor_is_withheld_from_her_agents_until_approved (Bob's anchor carries a label and name). bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test //crates/clax-server:integration__5: 2 tests pass; with the label/name lines removed from placeholder::anchor both fail (api_linked.rs:2552, anchor shows label 'Bob quoted this' and name 'Bob quoted this by name').","supersedes":"6fb4516bf3803b81087acf3e060272a6ff614cb16d3d2b2be89540617d35e73f","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:01:13.429410Z","id":"2f762425481cc476559624e08b00b09fb166aa3bdce2bd28c435ff841fab1651","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml. (Re-anchored: the figment rewrite of this file moved HostedConfig from lines 133:154.)","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":895},"end":{"line":916},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"4ef46d08062496dce479b254edb472278e981b7f22123e99d4ab1bb88f32e18f","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:01:13.452357Z","id":"05a0e0ca9ec8b1c057d4472f5bfb49d4e7ca0764c896457bac79fef02c76f57c","body":{"detail":"env_value reads `v = <raw>` as TOML first, so digits, true/false, dates and [..] become typed values; a string setting given such a value fails its table's check (turning that feature off) unless quoted (\"123\"). docs/contract.md (config.toml) states the rule, but a model ID or variable name made of digits would surprise.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":190},"end":{"line":200},"content_hash":"9ac0f4005307151a332425ebfc7e5d840b11453111439b2c8f4e6fbca8a6e4c5"},"suggested_fix":"Deserialize env values against the field's type (try the typed value, fall back to the raw string for String fields), as figment's lossy extraction does for some types.","summary":"An environment value that parses as TOML is not a string: CLAX_BOT__MODELS__DEFAULT=123 is an integer and its table refuses it","tags":["config","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:19:49.404763Z","id":"b0f2c02c8128c539518ddaffba7a4a2ac0f8047dcda2a363eefe69aab52b7491","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a6eee2e3","summary":"env_value now takes the setting's declared type from the defaults: a string setting takes the raw text (CLAX_BOT__MODELS__DEFAULT=123 is \"123\", CLAX_BOT__MODELS__COMPLEX=1.0 is \"1.0\"), integers still parse (CLAX_BOT__MAX_STEPS=5). Evidence: config::tests::an_environment_value_takes_its_settings_type passes in //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test (bazelisk test --nocache_test_results: PASSED).","supersedes":"05a0e0ca9ec8b1c057d4472f5bfb49d4e7ca0764c896457bac79fef02c76f57c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:19:49.474732Z","id":"b1285a35c9da6778188cb89eb173763e2fe4520756d9dddefcf80f57594430bd","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":957},"end":{"line":978},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"2f762425481cc476559624e08b00b09fb166aa3bdce2bd28c435ff841fab1651","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:30:08.469449Z","id":"a817cc58e60f4e275806cff2fcf00375378797cc61930c2c23afebd4ac4731ee","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":978},"end":{"line":999},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"b1285a35c9da6778188cb89eb173763e2fe4520756d9dddefcf80f57594430bd","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:30:15.878966Z","id":"bbda02db80d0cbdf01a9cf74e648e54e24510a91d8767ef04d0f3cfb0024daf2","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":989},"end":{"line":1010},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"a817cc58e60f4e275806cff2fcf00375378797cc61930c2c23afebd4ac4731ee","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.184376Z","id":"4ef1b6ab742460217e214e5d7f0c4c8843cf303f47c876ee79aab82dfac79a4b","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":997},"end":{"line":1018},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"bbda02db80d0cbdf01a9cf74e648e54e24510a91d8767ef04d0f3cfb0024daf2","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:15:16.476290Z","id":"d09d9662db632d8a4279ba0746cef6d215e177c49ae42882d182553bd933281c","body":{"detail":"The rule refuses IP literals, localhost, single labels and private suffixes. A name like key-sink.example.com resolving to 10.0.0.5 (or rebinding between checks) passes. On Cloudflare a Worker's fetch cannot reach private networks; a hosted native daemon has no such egress rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1274},"end":{"line":1307},"content_hash":"05e22d0196bc7327ec5f642b26149c381e833091ecac0bdf6613aba190a0c957"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted native daemon, resolve the host when sending and refuse private, loopback, link-local and unique-local answers (a reqwest resolver that filters them).","summary":"hosted_base_url_ok judges the URL's name, not where it resolves: a public-looking name whose DNS answers a private address still receives the key on a hosted native daemon","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.862594Z","id":"404e1e94da51475d1180e4dbf9ee1c94a7dcd5e09f75cc34f656b8fe908edb12","body":{"detail":"The rule refuses IP literals, localhost, single labels and private suffixes. A name like key-sink.example.com resolving to 10.0.0.5 (or rebinding between checks) passes. On Cloudflare a Worker's fetch cannot reach private networks; a hosted native daemon has no such egress rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1302},"end":{"line":1335},"content_hash":"05e22d0196bc7327ec5f642b26149c381e833091ecac0bdf6613aba190a0c957"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted native daemon, resolve the host when sending and refuse private, loopback, link-local and unique-local answers (a reqwest resolver that filters them).","summary":"hosted_base_url_ok judges the URL's name, not where it resolves: a public-looking name whose DNS answers a private address still receives the key on a hosted native daemon","supersedes":"d09d9662db632d8a4279ba0746cef6d215e177c49ae42882d182553bd933281c","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/anchor.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.357765Z","id":"8f5c1b832798047c45a06ce413c450c1158b5718bf38b6e05c42b7d814beedb2","body":{"detail":"An artifact anchor could keep the serde default file (index.html) and let the shell skip it by kind wherever it matches threads to the page shown: the pin numbering and resolve request in web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts (numbers, resolveAll, selectThread) and pinPlaces in web/shell/src/view/pins-model.ts. That puts code in the artifact entry, which is at its gzip budget, and says the thread is on the index when it is on no page. With file empty every 'is this thread on page X' test is already false, and holds('') is false, so selectThread leaves the frame alone; only the lazy sidebar model, the CLI's is_detached and the summary needed the kind.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":46},"content_hash":"725103793503edce275a0b1b4c87e30ea0156513acbd8424e83d38fe45bc5bd9"},"summary":"Whole-artifact anchors keep file index.html, with kind checks in the shell","supersedes":"93afd5ac8c780a1c47c30494a428a74153da243b8573252c1f6e38ce9f1bc60a","tags":["revisit:a reader of anchors needs every anchor's file to be a published path","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.412274Z","id":"6d332829cec6d7ad717758b9022e863185c26c00fd847b777243975dfad5826e","body":{"detail":"The rule refuses IP literals, localhost, single labels and private suffixes. A name like key-sink.example.com resolving to 10.0.0.5 (or rebinding between checks) passes. On Cloudflare a Worker's fetch cannot reach private networks; a hosted native daemon has no such egress rule.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1318},"end":{"line":1351},"content_hash":"05e22d0196bc7327ec5f642b26149c381e833091ecac0bdf6613aba190a0c957"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted native daemon, resolve the host when sending and refuse private, loopback, link-local and unique-local answers (a reqwest resolver that filters them).","summary":"hosted_base_url_ok judges the URL's name, not where it resolves: a public-looking name whose DNS answers a private address still receives the key on a hosted native daemon","supersedes":"404e1e94da51475d1180e4dbf9ee1c94a7dcd5e09f75cc34f656b8fe908edb12","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.470465Z","id":"1dfe0267e8420e6aa7cfe95e330fd79c90ef4942ca7d669bb2286c6e23bf20c8","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1013},"end":{"line":1034},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"4ef1b6ab742460217e214e5d7f0c4c8843cf303f47c876ee79aab82dfac79a4b","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.592681Z","id":"2b8dae9f964c58ddb6a5d9faa600ebee8a6d0afc06f9fd4b47779c79b5691abd","body":{"detail":"ReadTimeout, TaskFailed, NestedJob, WouldBlock and SchemaNewer (error.rs:60-91) describe only clax-store's executor (`clax_store::exec`) and migrations, so a change there edits clax-core's shared error type. Separately, no `just` recipe or Bazel target runs rustdoc with `-D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links` (grep -rn 'rustdoc' justfile scripts finds none), so links to items that move out of a crate (eight did, before being rewritten in plain backticks) are not caught. Moving the variants means a store error type that converts into CoreError at the HTTP boundary; adding the lane means a rustdoc build per crate in CI time.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":64},"end":{"line":95},"content_hash":"6349a18a1c9e410c95cfb43bfc8a7c95e2f81bb5dd44837160f8730fd31f9e91"},"summary":"CoreError holds clax-store's executor and migration failures, and no lane catches broken intra-doc links","supersedes":"af47d35f90bd678c2141177201838d6491ee956c6c950c395289140ca600a7a8","tags":["revisit:the next change to clax-store's executor errors, or when a rustdoc lane is added","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/seats.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:07.657616Z","id":"b989a4706c05f1263bc252ab68b152662ea005d99aa14ca39160a4822e4a6c83","body":{"detail":"Seats::take ORs the claim's reserved flag into the held seat and nothing clears it, so a person whose rights stop naming the artifact keeps a seat outside the pool until their last connection leaves or the seat goes idle; for that time the artifact seats one more person than SeatLimits::people. A share granted while seated is the mirror case: the seat stays counted against the pool until it is taken again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":395},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"22b83b7cb0b7e3c4447991cdead0cce6229e630f9bbe0057d502a7ef02616cd1"},"summary":"A seat taken as reserved stays reserved after the share that named the artifact is revoked","supersedes":"d910e3a59d8bf26ab25dd791f3339705de2caae165d3c435e50d831a29a5e1ac","tags":["live-seats","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:46.251622Z","id":"8ff717a26623f7247912b4cc8119266d5c6c81bb248a298b20a60da18ad275ec","body":{"detail":"MAX_SESSION_DRAFTS (8) keeps one session from holding every one of MAX_LIVE_DRAFTS (64), but an agent with the daemon token or a grant registers sessions freely, so eight sessions of one agent on 64 artifacts refuse every other draft (429 limit_reached) for as long as they revise every DRAFT_IDLE_SECS. A per-person or per-credential cap would close it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":270},"end":{"line":279},"content_hash":"529be8e04628b45becb412a7565ddb441dbedba28354b90bf6fa10916a4dcce1"},"summary":"Eight sessions still fill the 64 live drafts: session registration is not limited","supersedes":"dded3e3c5a75314f88ac7e9a501dd7be1311fc3dd414d17d7456ab41b3bf602a","tags":["drafts","limits","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/drafts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:38:46.802978Z","id":"4a5e10ee79381352f9318e950da97ea177fee26d746657414aaf00ee2aa9c2fb","body":{"detail":"MAX_LIVE_DRAFTS (64) times MAX_DRAFT_BYTES (1 MiB) are the daemon's limits, unchanged on wasm32, where the instance object shares 128 MB with every object in its isolate. One person with eight agent tokens (MAX_SESSION_DRAFTS 8 each) can fill them all.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"8bf0cba02fff43591fac18a5c7bf07493ade32239dbb38725f9b20398f860819"},"suggested_fix":"A smaller total on wasm32 (for example 16 live drafts) or a byte budget across live drafts.","summary":"Live drafts may hold 64 MiB on the Worker, half an isolate","supersedes":"129e50ba45d4ae89697a76abc8fca5cf9403e66792a3519043f7d4779bfcbfb8","tags":["worker","resource","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/publish.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-26T20:29:31.578147Z","id":"1b8aa5a919c64aeb196692ffa23e9e042334ab416ee1a51c3fbd48f2cb9d13b6","body":{"detail":"RestoreDeclaration::validated checks capabilities but versions:restore copies version n's files as they are, so a restore that passes capabilities different from n's clax.json records a version whose clax.json disagrees with its versions.capabilities_json. The Clax app passes the restored version's own declaration, which agrees; another caller need not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":140},"end":{"line":160},"content_hash":"aa14cfd48c933aa7d3d74dbb506774464800d57478a7e9335d1e53700104420e"},"suggested_fix":"In restore, write manifest::render(caps) as clax.json when capabilities is given, or refuse a capabilities that differs from n's clax.json with manifest_mismatch.","summary":"A restore with a capabilities field does not rewrite the restored version's clax.json","tags":["clax-json","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T03:36:58.597133Z","id":"23e564a177bcec0822d51138965a5649501bb0d67a667b71779a3a6b666b2968","body":{"detail":"ReadTimeout, TaskFailed, NestedJob, WouldBlock and SchemaNewer (error.rs:60-91) describe only clax-store's executor (`clax_store::exec`) and migrations, so a change there edits clax-core's shared error type. Separately, no `just` recipe or Bazel target runs rustdoc with `-D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links` (grep -rn 'rustdoc' justfile scripts finds none), so links to items that move out of a crate (eight did, before being rewritten in plain backticks) are not caught. Moving the variants means a store error type that converts into CoreError at the HTTP boundary; adding the lane means a rustdoc build per crate in CI time.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":68},"end":{"line":99},"content_hash":"6349a18a1c9e410c95cfb43bfc8a7c95e2f81bb5dd44837160f8730fd31f9e91"},"summary":"CoreError holds clax-store's executor and migration failures, and no lane catches broken intra-doc links","supersedes":"2b8dae9f964c58ddb6a5d9faa600ebee8a6d0afc06f9fd4b47779c79b5691abd","tags":["revisit:the next change to clax-store's executor errors, or when a rustdoc lane is added","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/capabilities.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T06:04:21.858699Z","id":"7989166400f7a1a1ec0d6297dd9d35160104bd565b6b164a14bdfefb475daee3","body":{"detail":"pending (via added) counts only new top-level names and new net hosts as additions. Once the account capability takes an `origins` list (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-26-quickstart-onboarding.md, task E: clax-core::capabilities::validate checks account.origins), a version that keeps `account` but lists more origins would be in force under the earlier approval without asking. Not done now because account.origins does not exist yet; task E adds it to added when it lands.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":228},"end":{"line":237},"content_hash":"36dfb93ce815ee6d05bdfa6a4cb16e7ec757e24a6ad261b7e294c9e645705314"},"summary":"Treat a widening of account.origins as an addition that waits for approval","tags":["revisit:E","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/scrub.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.357115Z","id":"aa28e54b3f766e6c2c1f99a2c8083f901433c741f8f9eccd21e6b6ee566bca46","body":{"detail":"url_at cuts up to two :<1-5 digits> groups off a URL's end as a stack frame's line and column when the character before them is not a digit (so ?card=4111:1111:1111 stays whole and is scrubbed as a query value). A query or path ending such as ?pin=x:12345 is cut the same way: :12345 is left outside the URL and so outside scrub_url's query scrubbing. web/sdk/src/scrub.ts urlAt reads the same; both suites share the case table.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":226},"end":{"line":260},"content_hash":"2b348995ae46e6725a7ca567cbebfa516b8bf08f4e6456b86eb33417757b1ce8"},"suggested_fix":"Cut a :line:column tail only after a path that ends in a script-like name (an extension), or only when the tail has two groups.","summary":"A URL ending in a colon and 1 to 5 digits after a non-digit keeps them unscrubbed in the path","tags":["feedback","scrub","privacy","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:15.180295Z","id":"c807323f837b2e2be6dd071d3b46dd58850f026ee8aacbb1c21ac868daa780ea","body":{"detail":"ClaxApp needs apple_team_id (the team that signs dev.empathic.clax for iOS and macOS), the SHA-256 fingerprint of the certificate that signs the Android release of dev.empathic.clax (Play App Signing's, if Google signs it), and the App Store and Play Store page URLs once the app is listed. Until they are set (Worker vars APPLE_TEAM_ID, ANDROID_PACKAGE, ANDROID_SHA256, IOS_STORE_URL, ANDROID_STORE_URL), /a/<id>/get offers only Open in Clax for Mac and Download .clax, and its link opens no app.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1189},"end":{"line":1219},"content_hash":"a4a8f124909c559b31c93c8c40e0fbeb64c084ca149204ba50d2d97649676c74"},"summary":"clax.dev's Apple team ID, Android signing fingerprint and store URLs are not chosen yet","supersedes":"c8dd99fbf998fa239253a42b9c093eee16e4d36aa4ad61d7da50b095f2d828c0","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:15.275799Z","id":"69a2dd23828f89ffc70a66ea587164aae9ca49f0d0c0a25778277a2dfbd7a69a","body":{"detail":"clax_server::hosted::Hosted::with_content_origin is set from the Worker's var (crates/clax-worker/src/instance.rs fn hosted) and by TestServer::spawn_hosted_with_content; a native hosted daemon behind its own proxy cannot set one in config.toml.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1156},"end":{"line":1177},"content_hash":"34f1facced5cb1258be31cc683f1d032558b320d983e7e37301b4b0ac685304e"},"summary":"[hosted] has no content_origin: only the Worker (CONTENT_ORIGIN) gives a hosted daemon a content origin of its own","supersedes":"1dfe0267e8420e6aa7cfe95e330fd79c90ef4942ca7d669bb2286c6e23bf20c8","tags":["hosted","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:15.372816Z","id":"a25514d6ffd24f30e52d6a48a1cbcbb155f59c3849181f9a234b266c5e18d90a","body":{"detail":"The rule refuses IP literals, localhost, single labels and private suffixes. A name like key-sink.example.com resolving to 10.0.0.5 (or rebinding between checks) passes. On Cloudflare a Worker's fetch cannot reach private networks; a hosted native daemon has no such egress rule.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1658},"end":{"line":1691},"content_hash":"05e22d0196bc7327ec5f642b26149c381e833091ecac0bdf6613aba190a0c957"},"suggested_fix":"On a hosted native daemon, resolve the host when sending and refuse private, loopback, link-local and unique-local answers (a reqwest resolver that filters them).","summary":"hosted_base_url_ok judges the URL's name, not where it resolves: a public-looking name whose DNS answers a private address still receives the key on a hosted native daemon","supersedes":"6d332829cec6d7ad717758b9022e863185c26c00fd847b777243975dfad5826e","tags":["hosted","security","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:15.661312Z","id":"15aa6368da2f40cb61f2b9ea310ad2d37d802e609704c61bb898f80797fc8a02","body":{"detail":"ReadTimeout, TaskFailed, NestedJob, WouldBlock and SchemaNewer (error.rs:60-91) describe only clax-store's executor (`clax_store::exec`) and migrations, so a change there edits clax-core's shared error type. Separately, no `just` recipe or Bazel target runs rustdoc with `-D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links` (grep -rn 'rustdoc' justfile scripts finds none), so links to items that move out of a crate (eight did, before being rewritten in plain backticks) are not caught. Moving the variants means a store error type that converts into CoreError at the HTTP boundary; adding the lane means a rustdoc build per crate in CI time.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"6349a18a1c9e410c95cfb43bfc8a7c95e2f81bb5dd44837160f8730fd31f9e91"},"summary":"CoreError holds clax-store's executor and migration failures, and no lane catches broken intra-doc links","supersedes":"23e564a177bcec0822d51138965a5649501bb0d67a667b71779a3a6b666b2968","tags":["revisit:the next change to clax-store's executor errors, or when a rustdoc lane is added","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/rights.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:15.752089Z","id":"1eccac19890caa7cfc0107132011d7fa1be20a84bb0a8dfb4e3e0967268def48","body":{"detail":"cap_raise drops from a raise only the actions a narrowing allows nowhere (and lowers db levels). A narrowing that allows an action at some artifacts only (made outside People, which narrows by whole actions: see the concern on web/shell/src/people/model.ts about whole actions) leaves that action on for a raise at any other artifact. Capping by location would cancel every raise at another person's artifact, because a narrowing is stated within the person's rights (Collaborator's update is at own), so the spec (§7.2) chose action and level; a narrowing that names artifacts would need its locations read as 'turned off elsewhere' to cap by place.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":755},"end":{"line":783},"content_hash":"bc434e4b793e424ca7b0c5d365ddd0bc580f61c5471491789526920668cbb6db"},"summary":"A narrowing caps a raise by action and db level, never by location","supersedes":"1fc0d7a04502ca3e21703d5939517685ad6308a9b60674e8aaafb3423ed9f784","tags":["spec:7.2","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/error.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:48.806989Z","id":"fc825abeac5dae5a9a29db91a353883331bbe61ed21256286e2a0b787eaeea00","body":{"detail":"`crate::Store` and `crate::Delivery` are clax-store items (the store moved out of clax-core; lib.rs:5 says the SQLite store is clax-store's). The intra-doc links that still name them do not resolve: error.rs:67 (`crate::Store::open_on`), content/mod.rs:4, :78, :423, :607 (`crate::Store`, `reconcile_pushes_async`, `call_async`), events.rs:69 and feedback.rs:77, :255 (`crate::Delivery::view`/`people`; clax-core's only Delivery is surface::Delivery, surface.rs:67, which has neither method). `grep -rn 'crate::Delivery\\|crate::Store' crates/clax-core/src` lists all eight. The variants ReadTimeout, TaskFailed, NestedJob, WouldBlock and SchemaNewer (error.rs:60-91) describe only clax-store's executor and migrations, so a change to that executor has to edit clax-core's shared error type.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:39187025-0a9f-4b13-8d2e-a1ea08e924ac)'s record.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":119},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"f44d3eb8c27f7aaae4fe51721517629bf65ef009f07560759450b4b18e838c59"},"suggested_fix":"Rewrite the eight links as `clax_store::Store::…` in plain backticks (clax-core cannot link to a crate above it), and add `cargo doc`/`bazel` rustdoc with `-D rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links` to a lane so the next move is caught.","summary":"Eight doc links in clax-core point at crate::Store and crate::Delivery, which this crate does not define, and the CoreError variants they document are clax-store's","supersedes":"a3465b4759601706886606b94f664a84e5d7ccaee8bd1db450fa11bc9eedcf59","tags":["review","review:deep-dive-2026-10-19","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/feedback.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:48.914622Z","id":"33bef9602d2f9d599bdfd3bb882470c37711987cb70636956050b47d0275206f","body":{"detail":"render_item knows a clip only through FeedbackItem::clip_path, which since 274f3832 is local_clip's path and so None for a Durable Object's or MemContent's clips; the item has no has_clip field, so a thread that has a clip reads to the agent as having none. The clip is served at /api/artifacts/<id>/threads/<tid>/clip either way.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":434},"end":{"line":445},"content_hash":"22eda8c287d504735f3991eddbcf09d4b72824a18fc7798ff5003bae679c395d"},"suggested_fix":"Carry has_clip (or the clip URL) on FeedbackItem and render 'Clip: at <url>' when there is no local file.","summary":"A clip kept in a content store with no local files renders as 'Clip: none (no screenshot was captured for this comment)'","supersedes":"6ded859508ff599fa0ec068eff3d15b88cc7e9e53cc234056472a772d6a1105f","tags":["content-store","wasm","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/gitctx_capture_tests.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:49.017935Z","id":"d8c3622d5af3d9c2e6cbf18ed80adb6120e46c5f10251811ffc1b547e22e17cc","body":{"detail":"In a bazelisk test of //crates/clax-core:clax_core_lib_test beside //crates/clax-store, //crates/clax-http and //crates/clax-server/... (2026-10-19), it failed at crates/clax-core/src/gitctx_capture_tests.rs:864 with '4 runs'; rerun alone (--cache_test_results=no) it passed. capture() under soon() may stop before its fifth git command when the machine is loaded, so the count depends on timing; asserting on the commands that ran, or capturing with no deadline, would remove it.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:b2fe0abc-990b-4628-b4c7-4c6d7f3f261b)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":844},"end":{"line":871},"content_hash":"631bc7f44ecf50aed47b3797cdb7553147dcd610b3b714bbc40a531176fef361"},"summary":"Load flake: every_command_runs_with_the_pins_and_a_cleared_environment saw 4 git runs where it asserts at least 5","supersedes":"f16b749c98631226db5d4d33c2d1103e6b43eec98cd005acbf51e8baa560d3ec","tags":["flake","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-core/src/visibility.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:49.131251Z","id":"73f38e9f0178a239c8309560a6d108ad18651a67f33fc20e9c49cf0804c3d0b9","body":{"detail":"authors_of_anchor names only the authors of the anchored file. The hosted client supplies the anchor text, and Store::mirror_thread (crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs:606-609) checks only its shape. The local file's author is the person, so the owner's agents read it. Bob, a stranger on the hosted Clax, can open a thread on Mia's app with up to 2000 characters of quote plus prefix, suffix, name and area text. Her local agents read that text through comments_read, GET .../threads and feedback items (anchor), while his comment body is withheld. Before afcdea2f2 the device read threads through the hosted agent channel. There the first comment of such a thread was withheld, so Sync::mirror (crates/clax-server/src/linked.rs first_seen) never brought the thread down. The same rule already lets a local unapproved person's anchor text reach the owner's agents (docs/contract.md:5331, 'a thread's anchor and clip the authors of the anchored file'). So whether a mirrored thread's anchor should also count its first commenter is a spec call.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":188},"end":{"line":201},"content_hash":"ee2add27242497ef136b62487d81a512380e504b3f06e03f3ec5c240f394ab3e"},"suggested_fix":"In authors_of_anchor, add the thread's first comment's remote_author when it has one, as authors_of_clip already does with the first commenter. A mirrored stranger's anchor is then withheld until the person approves that author.","summary":"A mirrored thread's anchor text (quote, prefix, suffix, name, area fingerprint) written by an unapproved hosted author reaches the local agents, because the anchor counts as the anchored file's authors","supersedes":"5af86ece9d19043d4d5f3bcbdd045c67d3082b7b11997f5d20302e83d1e1092d","tags":["security","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
